        "mechanism": "Abaloparatide exerts bone-anabolic effects through PTH1R RG-selective signaling: PTH1R RG Conformation Selectivity - Binds preferentially to the RG (G-protein-coupled, transient) conformation of PTH1R, producing brief cAMP pulses that activate osteoblastic bone formation pathways without prolonged signaling that would also stimulate osteoclasts Osteoblast Stimulation - Activates Gs-cAMP-PKA signaling in osteoblast lineage cells, upregulating Runx2, osterix, and osteocalcin gene expression; promotes osteoblast differentiation, matrix production, and mineralization Reduced R0 Engagement - Less activation of the R0 (prolonged signaling) conformation compared to teriparatide, resulting in less stimulation of RANKL expression and less secondary osteoclast activation Wider Anabolic Window - The ratio of bone formation to bone resorption stimulation is more favorable with abaloparatide, producing net bone accrual with less hypercalcemia Wnt Signaling Enhancement - Indirect upregulation of Wnt/β-catenin pathway through sclerostin reduction, amplifying osteoblast activity Trabecular and",
