        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Ac-SDKP (Goralatide) Chemical name N-Acetyl-seryl-aspartyl-lysyl-proline Molecular formula C₂₀H₃₃N₅O₉ Molecular weight 487.50 g/mol CAS number 110942-02-4 Sequence Ac-Ser-Asp-Lys-Pro Length 4 amino acids (N-acetylated tetrapeptide) Source Endogenous (N-terminal fragment of Thymosin Beta-4) Half-life ~5 minutes (rapidly hydrolyzed by ACE) Targets Hematopoietic stem cells; fibroblasts; inflammatory cells Bioavailability Subcutaneous, intravenous (research); oral (capsules, research) Legal status Research compound; not approved for therapeutic use Ac-SDKP (N-acetyl-seryl-aspartyl-lysyl-proline), also known by its investigational name Goralatide (or Seraspenide ), is an endogenous tetrapeptide derived from the enzymatic cleavage of the N-terminal four residues of Thymosin Beta-4 (Tβ4) by the serine protease prolyl oligopeptidase (POP).",
