        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3 Chemical name Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3 (Capixyl component) Molecular formula C₂₈H₄₇N₇O₇ Molecular weight 597.7 g/mol CAS number 827306-88-7 Sequence Ac-Gly-Lys-His-Lys-OH (4 amino acids with N-terminal acetylation) Length 4 amino acids (tetrapeptide targeting hair follicle extracellular matrix) Source Synthetic (developed by Lucas Meyer Cosmetics as key component of Capixyl) Half-life Enhanced stability from N-acetylation Targets Extracellular matrix proteins around hair follicle → stimulates collagen and laminin production → strengthens follicular anchorage; also inhibits 5-alpha-reductase Bioavailability Topical (scalp application); enhanced follicular penetration in Capixyl liposomal delivery Legal status Cosmeceutical ingredient (INCI: Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3); key component of Capixyl blend Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3 is a synthetic tetrapeptide that serves as the active peptide component of Capixyl , a widely-used anti-hair loss",
        "evidence": "Study Design Key Result Lucas Meyer Clinical 5% Capixyl lotion × 4 months, n=30 +13% anagen hairs; -29% telogen hairs; -46% total hair loss vs. placebo Collagen Synthesis In vitro - human dermal papilla cells 193% increase in collagen III; 121% increase in laminin-5 production DHT Inhibition In vitro - dermal papilla cells with Biochanin A 64% inhibition of 5-alpha-reductase; 68% reduction in DHT production Hair Pull Test Clinical, n=30, 4 months Significant reduction in hairs removed during standardized pull test 🧪 Vial Dex The World's Most Advanced Peptide Calculator 100% FREE 💧 Reconstitution Vial + BAC water mixing 📉 Dose & Units Syringe units to draw 🔀 Blend Multi-peptide vial ratios 📚 Stack Protocol Multi-vial dose planning 💨 Nasal Spray Spray bottle concentrations 50+ Peptides 7 Calculators 0 Signup Required Peptide: Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3 Open Free Calculator → [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Lucas Meyer Cosmetics Technical Data: Capixyl (Acetyl Tetrapeptide-3 + Trifolium Pratense Extract). Clariant Active Ingredients. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Katzer T, et al.",
