        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Acetyl Tetrapeptide-5 Chemical name Acetyl Tetrapeptide-5 (Eyeseryl) Molecular formula C₂₁H₃₅N₅O₈ Molecular weight 489.5 g/mol CAS number 820959-17-9 Sequence Ac-β-Ala-His-Ser-His-OH (4 amino acids; N-acetylated; contains beta-alanine) Length 4 amino acids (tetrapeptide targeting periorbital edema) Source Synthetic (Lipotec/Lubrizol); designed to reduce periorbital puffiness and under-eye bags Half-life Enhanced stability from N-terminal acetylation Targets Reduces vascular permeability → decreases fluid leakage from capillaries → reduces edema; also inhibits glycation Bioavailability Topical (primary route); designed for periorbital application Legal status Cosmeceutical ingredient (INCI: Acetyl Tetrapeptide-5; trade name Eyeseryl) Acetyl Tetrapeptide-5 (trade name Eyeseryl ) is a synthetic tetrapeptide developed by Lipotec specifically for reducing periorbital puffiness (under-eye bags), dark circles, and eye area edema.",
