        "mechanism": "ACTH exerts its primary effects through melanocortin 2 receptor (MC2R) on adrenal cortex cells: MC2R Activation in Adrenal CortexACTH binding to MC2R requires the accessory protein MRAP: - Activates adenylate cyclase and increases cAMP - Stimulates steroidogenic enzymes - Promotes cortisol synthesis and release - Also stimulates adrenal androgen production Cortisol-Mediated EffectsThe primary consequence of ACTH release is cortisol production: - Anti-inflammatory and immunomodulatory effects - Metabolic regulation (glucose, protein, fat) - Stress response adaptation - Feedback inhibition of ACTH release Direct Immunomodulatory EffectsACTH has effects beyond cortisol stimulation: - Immune cells express melanocortin receptors - Direct anti-inflammatory effects independent of cortisol - Modulation of cytokine production - These may explain efficacy in some conditions Melanocortin EffectsACTH has activity at other melanocortin receptors: - Some MC1R, MC3R, MC4R, MC5R activity - Contributes to skin pigmentation effects - Potential metabolic effects",
