        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Activin A Chemical name Activin A (Inhibin βA-βA homodimer) Molecular formula Homodimeric glycoprotein (two inhibin βA subunits) Molecular weight ~26,000 g/mol (mature homodimer) CAS number 104625-48-1 Sequence 116 amino acids per βA monomer (mature, human) Length 116 amino acids per subunit Source Endogenous (widespread); recombinant Half-life ~10-30 minutes (plasma; rapidly bound by follistatin) Targets ActRIIA/ActRIIB (Type II) + ALK4/ALK7 (Type I) → Smad2/3 signaling Bioavailability IV/local (research) Legal status Research compound; anti-activin antibodies in clinical development Activin A is a homodimeric glycoprotein member of the TGF-β superfamily, composed of two disulfide-linked inhibin βA subunits.",
        "evidence": "Essential for maintaining ESC/iPSC cultures in feeder-free conditions (Activin A + Wnt signaling) Gold standard for directing definitive endoderm differentiation in stem cell protocols Biomarker for preeclampsia (elevated in maternal serum) Biomarker for cancer cachexia severity and prognosis 🧪 Vial Dex The World's Most Advanced Peptide Calculator 100% FREE 💧 Reconstitution Vial + BAC water mixing 📉 Dose & Units Syringe units to draw 🔀 Blend Multi-peptide vial ratios 📚 Stack Protocol Multi-vial dose planning 💨 Nasal Spray Spray bottle concentrations 50+ Peptides 7 Calculators 0 Signup Required Peptide: Activin A Open Free Calculator → Well-tolerated at research doses High-dose systemic activin A: cachexia, muscle wasting, fibrosis (pathological) [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Namwanje M, Brown CW. \"Activins and inhibins: roles in development, physiology, and disease.\" Cold Spring Harb Perspect Biol . 2016;8:a021881. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Hoeper MM, et al. \"Sotatercept for PAH (STELLAR Trial).\" N Engl J Med . 2023;388:1478-1490. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Pearsall RS, et al.",
