        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Adamax Chemical name Adamantyl-Semax Analog Molecular formula C₄₉H₇₃N₁₁O₁₂ (approximate) Molecular weight ~1000 Da (estimated) CAS number N/A (research compound) Sequence Adamantyl-MEHFPGP (modified) Length 7 amino acids (with adamantane modification) Source Synthetic Half-life 4-8 hours (estimated, enhanced vs Semax) Targets Melanocortin receptors, BDNF/TrkB, NGF pathways Bioavailability Enhanced CNS penetration via adamantane moiety Legal status Research compound (unscheduled) Adamax is a synthetic nootropic peptide created by conjugating an adamantane (adamantyl) group to the N-terminus of Semax (MEHFPGP), a well-characterized heptapeptide analog of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH₄₋₁₀). The adamantane modification was designed to enhance blood-brain barrier (BBB) penetration, increase metabolic stability, and extend the biological half-life compared to unmodified Semax.",
        "evidence": "Route Dose Range Frequency Notes Intranasal 100-600 μg/day 1-2 times daily Analogous to Semax dosing with potentially longer intervals Subcutaneous 100-500 μg/day Once daily Enhanced stability allows subcutaneous route Note: Adamax dosing is extrapolated from Semax clinical data. No formal human clinical trials have been conducted. For community-tested protocols and dosing guidance, see PepDex Wiki . [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Ashmarin IP et al. (1995). \"Regulatory peptides in cognitive processes.\" Neurosci Behav Physiol . ↑ 2.0 2.1 Dolotov OV et al. (2006). \"Semax, an ACTH(4-10) analogue with nootropic properties, activates BDNF and trkB gene expression in rat hippocampus.\" Brain Res . ↑ 3.0 3.1 Grivennikov IA et al. (2008). \"Effects of Semax on expression of neurotrophic factors.\" Dokl Biol Sci . ↑ Liu J et al. (2013). \"Adamantane derivatives as potential therapeutic agents.\" Curr Med Chem . P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring.",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "Adamax shares the core mechanism of Semax while gaining pharmacokinetic advantages from the adamantane conjugation: Melanocortin Receptor Modulation - Like Semax, binds melanocortin MC3 and MC4 receptors, modulating attention, learning, and memory consolidation through cAMP/PKA signaling cascades BDNF Upregulation - Increases brain-derived neurotrophic factor expression in hippocampus and prefrontal cortex, promoting neuronal survival, synaptic plasticity, and long-term potentiation NGF Enhancement - Stimulates nerve growth factor production, supporting cholinergic neuron survival and function - critical for memory and attention TrkB Receptor Activation - BDNF-mediated activation of tropomyosin receptor kinase B triggers downstream MAPK/ERK and PI3K/Akt neuroprotective pathways Enhanced BBB Penetration - The adamantane group's high lipophilicity (LogP increase) facilitates transcellular transport across the blood-brain barrier, achieving higher CNS concentrations than unmodified Semax Proteolytic Resistance - N-terminal adamantane conjugation sterically protects against",
