        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia AgRP Chemical name Agouti-Related Peptide (AgRP, AGRP) Molecular formula C₅₇₆H₈₉₀N₁₆₂O₁₆₅S₁₂ (approximate, full-length) Molecular weight ~13,400 g/mol (full-length 132 aa); active fragment AgRP(83-132) ~5,600 g/mol CAS number 250612-89-2 (AgRP 83-132) Sequence Active fragment (83-132): CVRLHESCL...CRFFRSAC (50 aa; 5 disulfide bonds; ICK motif) Length 132 amino acids (full-length); 50 amino acids (active C-terminal fragment 83-132) Source Endogenous (AgRP/NPY neurons in arcuate nucleus of hypothalamus) Half-life ~4-8 hours (cystine-knot structure confers protease resistance) Targets Melanocortin-3 and -4 receptor (MC3R/MC4R) inverse agonist → blocks α-MSH anorexigenic signaling → promotes food intake Bioavailability ICV (research); not systemically administered Legal status Research compound (endogenous orexigenic peptide) Agouti-related peptide ( AgRP ) is a 132-amino acid neuropeptide that functions as the most potent and long-lasting",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Ollmann MM, et al. \"Antagonism of Central Melanocortin Receptors In Vitro and In Vivo by Agouti-Related Protein.\" Science . 1997;278:135-138. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Haskell-Luevano C, Monck EK. \"Agouti-Related Protein Functions as an Inverse Agonist at a Constitutively Active Brain Melanocortin-4 Receptor.\" Regul Pept . 2001;99:1-7. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Krashes MJ, et al. \"Rapid, Reversible Activation of AgRP Neurons Drives Feeding Behavior in Mice.\" J Clin Invest . 2011;121:1424-1428. ↑ Luquet S, et al. \"NPY/AgRP Neurons Are Essential for Feeding in Adult Mice but Can Be Ablated in Neonates.\" Science . 2005;310:683-685. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
