        "halfLifeContext": "PepCodex dossier summary. Route and species must be checked in the cited pharmacokinetic paper.",
        "mechanism": "Alixorexton acts as a replacement signal for the missing orexin in narcolepsy patients: OX2R Activation Selectively binds and activates orexin receptor 2 in wake-promoting brain regions, mimicking the natural orexin signal that is absent in NT1 patients. Neuronal Excitation Triggers Gq- protein signaling cascade leading to neuronal depolarization and increased firing in the tuberomammillary nucleus, locus coeruleus, and other arousal centers. Neurotransmitter Release Promotes release of histamine, norepinephrine, dopamine, and acetylcholine from wake-promoting neurons, collectively maintaining the wakeful state. Cataplexy Prevention Restores orexin-mediated inhibition of inappropriate muscle atonia during wakefulness, reducing sudden loss of muscle tone triggered by emotions.",
