        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Alpha-MSH Chemical name α-Melanocyte Stimulating Hormone Molecular formula C77H109N21O19S Molecular weight 1664.88 g/mol CAS number 581-05-5 Sequence Ac-Ser-Tyr-Ser-Met-Glu-His-Phe-Arg-Trp-Gly-Lys-Pro-Val-NH₂ Length 13 amino acids Source Natural POMC-derived hormone Half-life 7-20 minutes Targets Melanocortin receptors (MC1R-MC5R) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Research compound only Alpha-MSH (α-Melanocyte Stimulating Hormone) is a naturally occurring peptide hormone that serves as the body's primary regulator of melanocortin receptor signaling. Derived from the larger pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC) molecule, α-MSH plays crucial roles in skin pigmentation, appetite regulation, sexual arousal, and inflammatory responses. This tridecapeptide represents the prototype melanocortin agonist and has inspired the development of numerous synthetic analogs including Melanotan II and PT-141.",
