        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Amylin Chemical name Islet Amyloid Polypeptide (IAPP) Molecular formula C₁₆₅H₂₆₁N₅₁O₅₅S₂ Molecular weight 3903.3 g/mol CAS number 106602-62-4 Sequence KCNTATCATQRLANFLVHSSNNFGAILSSTNVGSNTY-NH₂ (disulfide Cys2-Cys7) Length 37 amino acids Source Pancreatic beta cells (co-secreted with insulin) Half-life ~15 minutes Targets Amylin receptors (CTR/RAMP complexes), Area postrema Bioavailability Endogenous Legal status Endogenous hormone Amylin (also known as Islet Amyloid Polypeptide or IAPP ) is a 37-amino acid peptide hormone co-secreted with insulin by pancreatic beta cells in response to nutrient stimulation. Discovered in 1987 by Per Westermark, amylin plays a critical complementary role to insulin in glucose homeostasis by slowing gastric emptying, suppressing postprandial glucagon secretion, and promoting satiety. Its synthetic analog pramlintide (Symlin) is FDA-approved for diabetes treatment.",
        "evidence": "Amylin potently reduces food intake and body weight in preclinical models Synergistic weight loss when combined with leptin (amylin restores leptin sensitivity) Basis for amylin/GLP-1 combination approaches ( Amycretin , CagriSema ) [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Westermark P, et al. \"Islet amyloid polypeptide, islet amyloid, and diabetes mellitus.\" Physiol Rev . 2011;91:795-826. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Hay DL, et al. \"Amylin: Pharmacology, Physiology, and Clinical Potential.\" Pharmacol Rev . 2015;67:564-600. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Lutz TA. \"Control of food intake and energy expenditure by amylin - therapeutic implications.\" Int J Obes . 2009;33:S24-S27. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
