        "mechanism": "Gastric Emptying : Potently slows gastric emptying, reducing the rate of glucose appearance in blood after meals Glucagon Suppression : Inhibits postprandial glucagon secretion from alpha cells (glucose-dependent) Satiety : Acts on area postrema and hypothalamic nuclei to promote meal termination and reduce food intake Glucose Regulation : Complements insulin's glucose-lowering effect through non-insulin mechanisms Bone Metabolism : Calcitonin-like effects via shared receptor components (CTR/RAMP) Amylin signals through heterodimeric receptors composed of the calcitonin receptor (CTR) complexed with receptor activity-modifying proteins (RAMP1, RAMP2, or RAMP3), forming AMY1, AMY2, and AMY3 receptors.",
