        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Antimicrobial Peptides (AMPs) are a diverse class of short peptides that form a critical component of innate immunity across all multicellular organisms. Also called host defense peptides (HDPs), AMPs kill bacteria, fungi, viruses, and parasites primarily through membrane disruption - a mechanism that makes resistance development far more difficult than with conventional antibiotics. With the global antibiotic resistance crisis intensifying, AMPs represent one of the most promising alternative therapeutic strategies. This article serves as a hub linking to all antimicrobial peptide articles on WikiPep.",
