        "mechanism": "AMPs kill microorganisms primarily through membrane disruption, using several models: Barrel-stave model - AMPs insert perpendicular to the membrane, forming transmembrane pores Toroidal pore model - AMPs bend the lipid bilayer inward, creating pores lined by both peptide and lipid Carpet model - AMPs accumulate on the membrane surface until reaching a critical concentration that causes membrane disintegration Some AMPs also have intracellular targets: DNA/RNA binding - Disrupting transcription and replication Ribosome inhibition - Blocking protein synthesis Cell wall synthesis interference - Targeting lipid II and other cell wall precursors",
