        "mechanism": "AOD-9604 works through mechanisms distinct from those of full growth hormone: Lipolysis StimulationAOD-9604 stimulates the breakdown of stored triglycerides in adipose tissue, releasing fatty acids into the bloodstream for use as energy. This lipolytic effect is similar to that of full growth hormone but occurs without stimulating IGF-1 production. Lipogenesis InhibitionThe peptide appears to inhibit the conversion of non-fat food sources into body fat, reducing the formation of new adipose tissue. This dual action-promoting fat breakdown while inhibiting fat storage-underlies its potential for body composition modification. Beta-3 Adrenergic Receptor InteractionResearch suggests AOD-9604 may interact with beta-3 adrenergic receptors, which are involved in fat metabolism and thermogenesis. This receptor pathway is distinct from growth hormone's primary signalling mechanisms. Glucose-Neutral EffectsUnlike full growth hormone, AOD-9604 does not appear to significantly affect blood glucose levels or insulin sensitivity in research to date.",
