        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "AOD-9604 is a synthetic peptide derived from the C-terminal end of human growth hormone - specifically amino acids 177 through 191 of the full HGH molecule. The \"AOD\" stands for Anti-Obesity Drug, which reflects exactly what it was engineered to be. The rationale was straightforward: full HGH produces two types of effects - anabolic tissue-building effects driven by IGF-1 elevation, and lipolytic fat-burning effects driven by a specific region of the HGH molecule. AOD-9604 is that lipolytic region, isolated and slightly modified, stripped of all the anabolic and glycemic machinery that makes full HGH complicated to use. The result is a compound that stimulates fat breakdown (lipolysis) in adipocytes and inhibits new fat formation (lipogenesis) through beta-3 adrenergic receptor pathways, without meaningfully raising IGF-1, without affecting blood glucose or insulin sensitivity, and without the tissue growth effects of full HGH.",
