        "summary": "ARA-290 (Cibinetide) is a non-hematopoietic erythropoietin (EPO) analogue engineered to remove EPO's erythropoietic (red blood cell-stimulating) activity while preserving its tissue-protective and anti-inflammatory signaling through the innate repair receptor (IRR). The IRR is a heterodimer of the EPO receptor (EPOR) and the common beta receptor (CD131) expressed on immune cells, neurons, and injured tissues - distinct from the classical EPOR homodimer that drives red blood cell production. ARA-290 binding to the IRR activates anti-inflammatory pathways including inhibition of NF-kB, reduction of pro-inflammatory cytokines (IL-1beta, TNF-alpha, IL-6), and stimulation of tissue repair signaling without thrombotic or erythropoietic side effects.",
