        "mechanism": "Argireline exerts its wrinkle-reducing effects through a sophisticated neuromodulatory mechanism that reduces facial muscle contraction intensity: SNARE Complex InhibitionThe core mechanism of Argireline involves interference with the SNARE (Soluble N-ethylmaleimide-sensitive factor Attachment protein REceptor ) complex-the molecular machinery essential for neurotransmitter release. The SNARE complex consists of three proteins: - SNAP-25: Located on the nerve terminal membrane - Syntaxin: Also on the nerve terminal membrane - VAMP/Synaptobrevin: Located on neurotransmitter vesicles These proteins must assemble correctly for vesicles containing acetylcholine (the neurotransmitter triggering muscle contraction) to fuse with the nerve terminal membrane and release their contents. SNAP-25 MimicryArgireline's sequence (Ac-EEMQRR-NH2) is designed to mimic the N-terminal region of SNAP-25. When present, Argireline competes with native SNAP-25 for incorporation into the SNARE complex.",
