        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Beinaglutide Chemical name Beinaglutide (recombinant human GLP-1(7-36)-NH₂) Molecular formula C₁₄₉H₂₂₅N₃₉O₄₆S Molecular weight 3355.7 g/mol CAS number Not assigned (biologic) Sequence His-Ala-Glu-Gly-Thr-Phe-Thr-Ser-Asp-Val-Ser-Ser-Tyr-Leu-Glu-Gly-Gln-Ala-Ala-Lys-Glu-Phe-Ile-Ala-Trp-Leu-Val-Lys-Gly-Arg-NH₂ Length 30 amino acids (GLP-1(7-36)-NH₂) Source Recombinant (E. coli expression, Shanghai Benemae) Half-life ~2-5 minutes (identical to native GLP-1; DPP-IV susceptible) Targets GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R) Bioavailability SC injection (three times daily) Legal status Approved in China (2017 - T2DM; 2023 - Obesity) Beinaglutide is a recombinant form of native human GLP-1(7-36)-NH₂ that is 100% identical in sequence to endogenous GLP-1.",
