        "summary": "Bronchogen is a synthetic tetrapeptide (Ala-Glu-Asp-Leu) Khavinson bioregulator derived from bronchial and lung tissue polypeptide extracts - identified as the bioactive core sequence responsible for the bronchial epithelial repair, respiratory mucosa regeneration, and pulmonary function-supporting activity of the native lung tissue extract. The respiratory epithelium that lines the bronchi, bronchioles, and alveoli is among the most exposed and metabolically stressed epithelial surfaces in the body: it encounters approximately 10,000-20,000 liters of air per day containing particulates, pathogens, oxidants, pollutants, and allergens while simultaneously maintaining the gas exchange efficiency, mucociliary clearance, and barrier function that protect the entire respiratory tract.",
