          "Severe active asthma exacerbation - the inflammatory and bronchospastic state of acute asthma represents a poor context for bronchial gene program normalization; Bronchogen is a maintenance/regenerative bioregulator, not an acute bronchodilator or anti-inflammatory.",
          "Known hypersensitivity to Bronchogen (Ala-Glu-Asp-Leu tetrapeptide) or formulation excipients.",
          "Pregnancy - respiratory epithelial bioregulator effects during pregnancy are not characterized.",
          "Severe pulmonary fibrosis in advanced stage - the end-stage fibrotic remodeling of severe pulmonary fibrosis represents a state where bronchial epithelial gene program normalization may have limited efficacy and uncertain interaction with the fibrotic process.",
          "Recent lung transplantation - bronchial epithelial bioregulator activity in immunosuppressed transplant recipients with donor lung epithelium requires transplant pulmonology supervision.",
          "Acute respiratory failure requiring ventilatory support - Bronchogen is not an acute intervention and is contraindicated as a treatment for active respiratory decompensation."
