        "summary": "A synthetic tripeptide (Ala-Glu-Asp) from Vladimir Khavinson's bioregulator framework, proposed to support cartilage tissue repair and chondrocyte function. All research originates from Russian institutes with no independent Western validation or controlled human clinical trials.",
        "evidence": "only single-group in-vitro (MSC/chondrocyte/fibroblast) and a few animal OA models; an unstructured mention of oral use in elderly OA patients lacks any described controlled design, so no creditable human tier. Mechanism: AED modulates Ki-67/CD98hc/MMP9/SASP markers in cell models but target is inferred with no binding/knockout validation. Plausibility: chondrogenic-marker (SOX9, COL2, aggrecan) coherence is decent though mechanism-to-cartilage-outcome links remain unproven. Global coverage: all work originates from the Khavinson/Linkova St. Petersburg group with no independent or non-Russian replication. Community experience: negligible - no meaningful user reports. Effectiveness not-established: no quantified human efficacy estimate and no meaningful community effect signal.",
