        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17T07:28:51+00:00",
        "summary": "09 How This Works Cartalax (Ala‑Glu‑Asp) is classified among the Khavinson bioregulatory peptides-ultrashort peptides that may interact with DNA and modulate gene expression at nanomolar concentrations [1] [4] . The peptide sequence corresponds to a motif found in the alpha‑1 chain of type XI collagen, a structural protein important for cartilage integrity [5] . In preclinical fibroblast and chondrocyte culture models, Cartalax has been reported to upregulate Ki‑67 (a proliferation marker), increase SIRT‑1/SIRT‑6 expression, reduce p53 and caspase‑3 activity (pro‑apoptotic signals), and inhibit MMP‑9 synthesis (an enzyme linked to extracellular matrix degradation) [2] [3] [6] .",
