        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia CGRP Chemical name Calcitonin Gene-Related Peptide Molecular formula C₁₈₆H₂₉₁N₅₅O₅₇S₂ (alpha-CGRP) Molecular weight 3789.4 g/mol CAS number 83652-28-2 Sequence ACDTATCVTHRLAGLLSRSGGVVKNNFVPTNVGSKAF-NH₂ (alpha-CGRP) Length 37 amino acids Source Sensory neurons (alternative splicing of calcitonin gene) Half-life ~7 minutes Targets CGRP receptor (CLR/RAMP1 complex) Bioavailability Endogenous neuropeptide Legal status Endogenous / Target of approved drugs CGRP ( Calcitonin Gene-Related Peptide ) is a 37-amino acid neuropeptide produced by alternative RNA splicing of the calcitonin/CGRP gene (CALCA) in sensory neurons. It is one of the most potent vasodilators known and plays a central role in migraine pathophysiology, pain transmission, and neurogenic inflammation. Two isoforms exist: alpha-CGRP (predominantly neural) and beta-CGRP (from a separate gene, CALCB, predominantly enteric).",
        "evidence": "Goadsby PJ, et al. (1990): Demonstrated elevated CGRP in jugular blood during migraine Lassen LH, et al. (2002): CGRP infusion triggers migraine in patients Multiple Phase 3 trials (2017-2023): Anti-CGRP antibodies and gepants validated as effective migraine therapies CGRP's role in cluster headache, medication-overuse headache CGRP and cardiovascular risk (concern about blocking a vasodilator) CGRP in irritable bowel syndrome and inflammatory bowel disease CGRP-based diagnostics for migraine [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Russell FA, et al. \"Calcitonin gene-related peptide: physiology and pathophysiology.\" Physiol Rev . 2014;94:1099-1142. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Goadsby PJ, et al. \"Pathophysiology of migraine: a disorder of sensory processing.\" Physiol Rev . 2017;97:553-622. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Edvinsson L, et al. \"CGRP as the target of new migraine therapies.\" Nat Rev Neurol . 2018;14:338-350. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring.",
