        "mechanism": "Vasodilation : Most potent endogenous vasodilator known (~1000x more potent than substance P); acts on vascular smooth muscle via cAMP elevation Neurogenic Inflammation : Released from trigeminal sensory neurons during migraine; causes mast cell degranulation, plasma extravasation, and dural inflammation Pain Transmission : Facilitates nociceptive signaling in trigeminal ganglion and spinal dorsal horn Central Sensitization : Promotes central pain sensitization in chronic migraine Receptor Complex : Signals through heterodimer of calcitonin receptor-like receptor (CLR) and RAMP1",
