        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia CJC-1293 Chemical name CJC-1293 (Modified GRF 1-29; predecessor to CJC-1295 without DAC) Molecular formula C₁₅₂H₂₅₂N₄₄O₄₂ Molecular weight 3367.9 g/mol CAS number Research compound Sequence Tyr-D-Ala-Asp-Ala-Ile-Phe-Thr-Gln-Ser-Tyr-Arg-Lys-Val-Leu-Ala-Gln-Leu-Ser-Ala-Arg-Lys-Leu-Leu-Gln-Asp-Ile-Leu-Ser-Arg-NH₂ (29 aa; modified GHRH 1-29 with 4 amino acid substitutions for stability) Length 29 amino acids (modified GHRH 1-29 with 4 substitutions: positions 2, 8, 15, 27 for DPP-IV resistance) Source Synthetic (modified GHRH 1-29; precursor compound to CJC-1295; developed by ConjuChem Biotechnologies) Half-life ~30 minutes (without DAC; much shorter than CJC-1295 with DAC which is ~8 days) Targets GHRH receptor (Gs-coupled) → cAMP → GH release from pituitary somatotropes; identical receptor target as endogenous GHRH Bioavailability SC injection (community use); IV (research) Legal status Research compound (precursor to CJC-1295; used extensively in",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Jetté L, et al. \"hGRF1-29-Albumin Bioconjugates Activate the GRF Receptor on the Anterior Pituitary in Rats: Identification of CJC-1295 as a Long-Lasting GRF Analog.\" Endocrinology . 2005;146:3052-3058. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Teichman SL, et al. \"Prolonged Stimulation of Growth Hormone (GH) and Insulin-Like Growth Factor I Secretion by CJC-1295, a Long-Acting Analog of GH-Releasing Hormone, in Healthy Adults.\" J Clin Endocrinol Metab . 2006;91:799-805. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Bowers CY. \"Growth Hormone-Releasing Peptide (GHRP).\" Cell Mol Life Sci . 1998;54:1316-1329. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises). Saturation Tracking Half-Life Curves AI Coach 24hr Free Trial Try Free for 24 Hours → Retrieved from \" https://wikipep.org/index.php?title=CJC-1293&oldid=3852 \" Categories : Peptides GHRH Analogs Growth Hormone Secretagogues Research Peptides Anti-Aging Peptides CJC-1293 Add topic",
