        "mechanism": "GHRH Receptor Agonism : Binds GHRH receptor on pituitary somatotropes → Gs → cAMP → PKA → GH gene transcription and GH secretion DPP-IV Resistance : 4 amino acid substitutions (positions 2, 8, 15, 27) block DPP-IV cleavage → half-life extended from ~7 minutes (native GHRH) to ~30 minutes Pulsatile GH Release : Without DAC, GH release follows natural pulse pattern → physiological GH profile GHRP Synergy : Maximum GH release when combined with a GHRP ( Ipamorelin , GHRP-2, etc.) → GHRH \"loads the gun,\" GHRP \"pulls the trigger\" Somatotrope Health : Maintains and may increase the number of pituitary somatotropes (GH-producing cells)",
