        "url": "https://pepuniversity.com/peptide-codex.php#cjc-1295-dac",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "CJC-1295 DAC is the long-acting version of the CJC GHRH analog family. The DAC - Drug Affinity Complex - is a chemical modification that causes the peptide to covalently bind to serum albumin immediately upon injection. Albumin is the most abundant protein in blood plasma, and binding to it transforms CJC-1295 DAC from a peptide that would otherwise clear in 30 minutes into one that recirculates for approximately 8 days. The practical consequence is that a single or twice-weekly injection maintains continuously elevated GH and IGF-1 levels around the clock, rather than producing the timed pulsatile surges that CJC-1295 No DAC creates. This is the fundamental pharmacological split between the two CJC variants: No DAC restores natural GH pulse physiology, DAC replaces it with a steady hormonal \"bleed.\" Strict fasting is not required with DAC because the GH elevation is not timed to a peak - it is sustained at all times regardless of feeding status.",
        "evidence": "Peptide University labels its records as aggregated from empirical research and anecdotal community data. This record is retained as supplied and is not upgraded to clinical evidence.",
        "halfLife": "",
