        "url": "https://pepuniversity.com/peptide-codex.php#cjc-1295-no-dac",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "CJC-1295 (No DAC), also known as Modified GRF 1-29, is a synthetic analog of the first 29 amino acids of endogenous Growth Hormone Releasing Hormone (GHRH). The human body normally releases GHRH in discrete pulses from the hypothalamus, which travel to the anterior pituitary and trigger timed bursts of growth hormone secretion. The problem with native GHRH is that it is destroyed by dipeptidyl peptidase-IV (DPP-IV) enzymes within minutes of release, making it useless as a therapeutic agent without modification. CJC-1295 (No DAC) solves this with four strategic amino acid substitutions at positions 2, 8, 15, and 27 that block DPP-IV cleavage - extending the half-life from under 2 minutes to approximately 30 minutes while preserving the precise GHRH receptor binding profile. The result is a compound that accurately mimics the body's natural GH pulse physiology: a short, sharp burst of pituitary GH secretion rather than a sustained elevation.",
