        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia CNP Chemical name C-type Natriuretic Peptide (CNP-22; CNP-53) Molecular formula C₁₀₆H₁₇₀N₃₂O₃₁S₂ (CNP-22) Molecular weight 2197.4 g/mol (CNP-22); 5802 g/mol (CNP-53) CAS number 127869-51-6 (CNP-22) Sequence GLSKGCFGLKLDRIGSMSGLGC (22 aa; single disulfide ring; no C-terminal extension) Length 22 amino acids (CNP-22) or 53 amino acids (CNP-53; the predominant active form) Source Endogenous (endothelial cells, brain, cartilage growth plate chondrocytes, heart) Half-life ~2-3 minutes (rapid neutral endopeptidase/NEP degradation; shortest-lived natriuretic peptide) Targets NPR-B (natriuretic peptide receptor B) → guanylyl cyclase → cGMP → vasodilation, bone growth, anti-fibrosis Bioavailability IV infusion (research); analog vosoritide is SC (FDA-approved) Legal status Endogenous peptide; analog Vosoritide (TransCon CNP) FDA-approved for achondroplasia (2021) C-type Natriuretic Peptide (CNP) is the third member of the natriuretic peptide family",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Sudoh T, et al. \"C-Type Natriuretic Peptide (CNP): A New Member of Natriuretic Peptide Family Identified in Porcine Brain.\" Biochem Biophys Res Commun . 1990;168:863-870. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Savarirayan R, et al. \"C-Type Natriuretic Peptide Analogue Therapy in Children with Achondroplasia.\" N Engl J Med . 2019;381:25-35. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Savarirayan R, et al. \"Once-Daily, Subcutaneous Vosoritide Therapy in Children with Achondroplasia: A Randomised, Double-Blind, Phase 3, Placebo-Controlled, Multicentre Trial.\" Lancet . 2020;396:684-692. ↑ Potter LR, et al. \"Natriuretic Peptides, Their Receptors, and Cyclic Guanosine Monophosphate-Dependent Signaling Functions.\" Endocr Rev . 2006;27:47-72. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
