        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Colostrinin Chemical name Colostrinin (CLN; Proline-Rich Polypeptide Complex; PRP) Molecular formula Complex mixture (multiple proline-rich peptides; ~6-40 amino acids each) Molecular weight ~500-3000 g/mol (complex of proline-rich peptides; predominant fraction ~6 kDa) CAS number 173392-90-4 Sequence Complex mixture of proline-rich peptides (predominant peptide: ~34 amino acids with high proline content; from ovine colostrum) Length Variable (mixture of proline-rich peptides from 6-40 amino acids; the \"active fraction\" of colostrum) Source Natural (isolated from ovine/sheep colostrum - the first milk produced after birth; rich in immunomodulatory peptides) Half-life Variable (complex mixture; proline-rich peptides are moderately resistant to proteolysis) Targets Multiple - immunomodulatory (cytokine regulation), antioxidant (ROS scavenging), anti-amyloid (Aβ aggregation inhibition) Bioavailability Oral (marketed as oral supplement; proline-rich",
        "evidence": "Trial Population N Duration Key Result Leszek et al. (2002) Mild-moderate AD 46 30 weeks Cognitive stabilization in 40% of colostrinin group vs. progressive deterioration in 65% of placebo Bilikiewicz & Gaus (2004) Mild-moderate AD 105 15 months Stabilization of ADAS-cog scores; modest but significant benefit vs. placebo (p<0.05) Leszek et al. (1999) Mild-moderate AD 46 15 weeks (open) 33% of patients showed MMSE improvement; 40% stabilized [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Janusz M, Lisowski J. \"Proline-Rich Polypeptide (PRP) - An Immunomodulatory Peptide from Ovine Colostrum.\" Arch Immunol Ther Exp . 1993;41:275-279. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Leszek J, et al. \"Colostrinin: A Proline-Rich Polypeptide (PRP) Complex Isolated from Ovine Colostrum for Treatment of Alzheimer's Disease.\" J Alzheimers Dis . 2002;4:531-536. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Bilikiewicz A, Gaus W. \"Colostrinin (a Naturally Occurring, Proline-Rich, Polypeptide Mixture) in the Treatment of Alzheimer's Disease.\" J Alzheimers Dis . 2004;6:17-26. ↑ Boldogh I, Bhasklar K. \"Colostrinin, a molecular chaperone with anti-amyloidogenic activity.\"",
        "halfLife": "",
