        "mechanism": "Immunomodulation : Bidirectional - stimulates Th1 cytokines when suppressed (infection, immunosenescence); suppresses Th1/Th17 when overactivated (autoimmune states) Cytokine Regulation : Normalizes TNF-α, IFN-γ, IL-6, and IL-10 production toward physiological ratios → balanced immune response Anti-Amyloid : Inhibits Aβ₁₋₄₂ peptide aggregation and fibril formation in vitro; may redirect Aβ toward non-toxic oligomeric forms Antioxidant : Reduces oxidative stress markers (4-HNE, lipid peroxidation, ROS) in neuronal cell cultures; increases glutathione (GSH) Neuroprotection : Protects neurons from Aβ-induced and H₂O₂-induced apoptosis via mitochondrial stabilization Nitric Oxide Regulation : Modulates inducible nitric oxide synthase (iNOS) expression → prevents excessive NO production that causes neuronal damage Sirtuin Activation : Some evidence for SIRT1 upregulation → NAD+-dependent deacetylase linked to longevity and neuroprotection Proteasome Enhancement : Restores proteasome activity in aged cells → improved clearance of damaged/aggregated proteins",
        "limitations": [],
