        "summary": "Cortagen is a synthetic tripeptide bioregulator (EDR: Glutamic acid-Aspartic acid-Arginine) developed by Professor Vladimir Khavinsky at the St. Petersburg Institute of Bioregulation and Gerontology, specifically targeting neuroprotection and functional restoration of cerebral cortex neurons. Cortagen is structurally related to Pinealon (also an EDR-sequence peptide), but the two are formulated for distinct brain regions: Pinealon targets hippocampal memory consolidation and pineal gland neurogenesis, while Cortagen targets the cerebral cortex - higher cognitive function, executive processing, and cortical neuroprotection against age-related decline. Cortagen's mechanism operates through the same epigenetic gene regulation pathway as Pinealon: it penetrates cell nuclei and modulates transcription factor activity, influencing the expression of genes governing neuronal survival, neurotrophin production, and anti-apoptotic signaling in cortical tissue.",
