        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Cotadutide Chemical name Cotadutide (MEDI0382) Molecular formula Modified GLP-1/glucagon peptide (acylated) Molecular weight ~4,100 Da (estimated) CAS number 1757458-81-7 Sequence Proprietary GLP-1/glucagon dual agonist (acylated) Length ~30 amino acids (estimated) Source Synthetic Half-life ~5 days (acylation-mediated albumin binding) Targets GLP-1 receptor (agonist) + Glucagon receptor (agonist) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Investigational (Phase 2b/3) Cotadutide (development code MEDI0382 ) is a dual GLP-1/glucagon receptor agonist being developed by AstraZeneca for the treatment of metabolic dysfunction-associated steatohepatitis (MASH/NASH) , obesity , and type 2 diabetes .",
        "evidence": "Route Frequency Titration Target Dose Subcutaneous Once daily (current) or weekly (extended formulations in development) Gradual escalation over 4-8 weeks 300-600 μg/day (dose-finding ongoing) [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Ambery P, et al. \"MEDI0382, a GLP-1 and glucagon receptor dual agonist, in obese or overweight patients with type 2 diabetes.\" Lancet . 2018;391(10140):2607-2618. ↑ 2.0 2.1 AstraZeneca. \"Cotadutide clinical development update.\" Corporate presentations 2023-2024. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Day JW, et al. \"A new glucagon and GLP-1 co-agonist eliminates obesity in rodents.\" Nat Chem Biol . 2009;5:749-757. ↑ Parker VER, et al. \"Cotadutide promotes liver fat reduction and weight loss.\" Diabetes Obes Metab . 2020. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
        "halfLife": "",
