        "summary": "Crystagen is a synthetic tripeptide (Lys-Glu-Asp) Khavinson bioregulator derived from immune system tissue polypeptide extracts with primary activity on the peripheral adaptive and innate immune compartments - specifically targeting natural killer (NK) cells, macrophages, T-lymphocytes, and B-lymphocytes as the primary effector cell populations of systemic immune defense. While Vilon (also in this database) focuses specifically on the thymic arm of immune function - the production and maturation of naive T-cells from the thymic epithelium - Crystagen operates downstream at the peripheral immune effector level, targeting the already-matured immune cell populations in the blood, lymph nodes, and peripheral tissues that carry out surveillance, pathogen clearance, and immune regulation.",
