        "mechanism": "CT-388 activates two hormone receptors simultaneously to reduce appetite and improve metabolism: GLP-1 Receptor Signals fullness to the brain, slows stomach emptying , and enhances glucose-dependent insulin release from the pancreas. GIP Receptor Synergizes with GLP-1 for enhanced insulin secretion and directly improves fat cell function and lipid metabolism. Appetite Control Dual receptor activation creates stronger satiety signals than single-receptor drugs, leading to reduced food intake. Metabolic Effects Improves insulin sensitivity, reduces blood glucose levels, and may improve lipid profiles through multiple pathways.",
