        "mechanism": "CT-388 activates both incretin receptor pathways through its dual agonist design: GLP-1 Receptor Agonism - Activates GLP-1R on pancreatic β-cells (glucose-dependent insulin secretion, β-cell preservation), hypothalamic neurons (appetite suppression via POMC/CART activation), vagal afferents (satiety signaling), and gastric smooth muscle (delayed emptying) GIP Receptor Agonism - Activates GIPR on pancreatic β-cells (synergistic insulin potentiation), adipocytes (enhanced lipid metabolism), and brain (emerging evidence for direct central appetite effects); GIP/GLP-1 co-agonism produces greater weight loss than GLP-1 alone Synergistic Incretin Effect - Dual pathway activation recruits complementary metabolic circuits: GLP-1 primarily drives appetite suppression while GIP modulates adipose tissue function and lipid handling, producing additive/synergistic weight loss Beta-Cell Preservation - Combined GLP-1/GIP signaling provides enhanced anti-apoptotic protection for pancreatic β-cells through parallel cAMP/PKA and PI3K/Akt pathways, potentially slowing type 2 diabetes progression",
