        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Danuglipron Chemical name Danuglipron (PF-06882961) Molecular formula C₂₈H₂₆F₃N₃O₅ Molecular weight 545.5 g/mol CAS number 2221035-64-3 Sequence Non-peptide small molecule (GLP-1R agonist) Length N/A (small molecule) Source Synthetic (Pfizer) Half-life ~6-8 hours (IR); extended with MR formulation Targets GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R) Bioavailability Oral (small molecule) Legal status Investigational (Phase 2/3) Danuglipron (development code PF-06882961 ) is an investigational oral, non-peptide, small-molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist being developed by Pfizer. Unlike all currently approved GLP-1 receptor agonists which are injectable peptides (or oral peptide formulations like oral semaglutide requiring the SNAC absorption enhancer), danuglipron is a true small molecule that can be manufactured using standard pharmaceutical chemistry at potentially much lower cost than peptide-based therapies.",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Pfizer. \"Danuglipron Phase 2b Results in Obesity.\" Presented at ADA Scientific Sessions. 2023. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Saxena AR, et al. \"Danuglipron, a novel oral GLP-1 receptor agonist: Phase 2 results.\" Lancet . 2023. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Griffith DA, et al. \"A small-molecule oral agonist of the human glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor.\" J Med Chem . 2022;65:8208-8226. ↑ Coskun T, et al. \"Oral small molecule GLP-1 receptor agonists: current landscape.\" Trends Pharmacol Sci . 2024. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises). Saturation Tracking Half-Life Curves AI Coach 24hr Free Trial Try Free for 24 Hours → Retrieved from \" https://wikipep.org/index.php?title=Danuglipron&oldid=3878 \" Categories : Peptides GLP-1 Receptor Agonists Oral Small Molecules Investigational Drugs Metabolic Therapeutics Danuglipron Add topic",
