        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Daptomycin (Cubicin) Chemical name Daptomycin; LY 146032 Molecular formula C₇₂H₁₀₁N₁₇O₂₆ Molecular weight 1620.67 g/mol CAS number 103060-53-3 Sequence Cyclic lipopeptide: 13 amino acids with a decanoyl lipid tail; Trp-D-Asn-Asp-Thr-Gly-Orn-Asp-D-Ala-Asp-Gly-D-Ser-3MeGlu-Kyn Length 13 amino acids (cyclic lipodepsipeptide) Source Natural product from Streptomyces roseosporus Half-life 8-9 hours (enabling once-daily dosing) Targets Bacterial cell membrane (calcium-dependent membrane insertion); cell wall precursor lipids Bioavailability ~92% (IV administration); not orally bioavailable Legal status FDA Approved (2003); EMA Approved; Prescription only Daptomycin , marketed under the brand name Cubicin (Merck, formerly Cubist Pharmaceuticals), is a cyclic lipopeptide antibiotic produced naturally by the soil bacterium Streptomyces roseosporus .",
        "evidence": "Left-sided endocarditis: Higher doses (8-12 mg/kg) used in clinical practice Prosthetic joint infections: Component of combination therapy Bone and joint infections: Particularly MRSA osteomyelitis Central nervous system infections: Limited penetration but used in ventriculitis/meningitis with intraventricular administration VRE infections: Bacteremia and other serious infections cSSSI Trials: Two Phase III trials demonstrated non-inferiority to vancomycin/semisynthetic penicillins with a 4-day shorter median treatment duration SAB/Endocarditis Trial: CORE study demonstrated non-inferiority to standard therapy (anti-staphylococcal penicillin or vancomycin + gentamicin) Dose Optimization: Studies evaluating high-dose daptomycin (10-12 mg/kg) for improved outcomes Combination Therapy: Daptomycin plus beta-lactam synergy (the \"seesaw effect\" - beta-lactam exposure enhances daptomycin activity in some resistant strains) New Lipopeptide Development: Daptomycin analogs with improved properties (e.g., surotomycin, CB-182,804) Anti-Biofilm Activity: Investigation of daptomycin's efficacy",
