        "mechanism": "Tyrosinase Inhibition : Competitively binds the active site of human tyrosinase → blocks conversion of L-tyrosine → L-DOPA → dopaquinone (the rate-limiting steps of melanogenesis) Non-Cytotoxic : Does not kill melanocytes (unlike hydroquinone at high concentrations) - inhibits enzyme without affecting cell viability Selective : High specificity for tyrosinase - does not broadly inhibit other copper-containing enzymes Melanin Production Reduction : Reduces melanin synthesis in melanocytes → gradual lightening of hyperpigmented areas Epidermal Targeting : Small peptide penetrates stratum corneum to reach melanocytes in the basal layer No Ochronosis Risk : Unlike hydroquinone, no risk of paradoxical darkening (exogenous ochronosis) with long-term use",
        "limitations": [],
