        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Dihexa (PNB-0408) is a synthetic peptide derived from angiotensin IV - modified at both ends to dramatically improve its ability to cross the blood-brain barrier and survive oral digestion. Where most cognitive peptides target neurotransmitter systems or protect existing neurons, Dihexa works at a more fundamental level: it acts as a potent amplifier of HGF (hepatocyte growth factor) at the c-Met receptor in the brain, triggering the formation of entirely new synaptic connections - a process called synaptogenesis. This mechanism is responsible for its reputation as one of the most potent neuroplasticity compounds ever studied. Preclinical models have shown Dihexa fully reversing induced memory deficits and improving cognitive performance in aged subjects - effects that required doses orders of magnitude lower than other known synaptogenic agents.",
