        "lastReviewed": "Not stated",
        "summary": "DIA-39-C20 (Dual Regulator) is a 39-amino acid dual incretin agonist belonging to the Peptide Receptor Modulator Research Series. It simultaneously targets both the GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R) and the GIP receptor (GIPR), producing synergistic - not merely additive - metabolic effects through co-activation of overlapping downstream signaling pathways. The backbone is engineered from a GIP-based scaffold with Aib substitutions at positions 2 and 13 for DPP-4 resistance, and carries a C20 fatty diacid (eicosanedioyl) side chain via a γ-Glu-2x AEEA linker for albumin binding and extended once-weekly half-life. CAS: 2023788-19-2. Structurally analogous in class to tirzepatide. Once-weekly subcutaneous injection. Key reference literature: Coskun et al. (Cell Metabolism 2022) - LY3437943 triple receptor agonist, discovery to clinical proof; Urva et al. (Lancet 2022) - Phase 1b multiple-ascending dose trial; Jastreboff et al.",
