        "summary": "Epithalon (epitalon) is a synthetic tetrapeptide (Ala-Glu-Asp-Gly) derived from epithalamin, a natural polypeptide produced by the pineal gland. Its primary researched mechanism is activation of telomerase - the enzyme responsible for maintaining and extending the protective telomere caps at the ends of DNA strands. Telomeres shorten with each cell division; critically shortened telomeres trigger cellular senescence. Epithalon is one of only a small number of compounds that has demonstrated telomerase activation in both in vitro and animal studies, positioning it as a significant subject of longevity research. Secondary mechanisms include restoration of melatonin secretion via pineal gland normalization, antioxidant activity, and modulation of neuroendocrine function. In Russian research spanning over 30 years, Epithalon-treated animals showed increased lifespan, reduced tumor incidence, and improved physiological markers of aging. Human studies remain limited.",
