        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Follistatin 315 Chemical name Follistatin 315 (FS315 / FST315) Molecular formula Glycoprotein (315 amino acids + glycosylation) Molecular weight ~38,000 g/mol (unglycosylated); ~45-50 kDa glycosylated CAS number 136470-06-5 Sequence 315 amino acids (full-length human follistatin, includes heparin-binding sequence) Length 315 amino acids Source Endogenous (liver, ovary, muscle, pituitary); recombinant Half-life ~2-4 hours (longer than FS288 due to lower heparin binding) Targets Activin A/B (primary); myostatin/GDF-8; GDF-11; BMP-2/4/6/7 (all sequestered/neutralized) Bioavailability IV/SC (research); Gene therapy (AAV-follistatin) Legal status Research compound; gene therapy in clinical trials Follistatin 315 ( FS315 or FST315 ) is the predominant circulating isoform of follistatin - a single-chain glycoprotein that functions as an endogenous antagonist of activin A, myostatin (GDF-8), and other TGF-β superfamily ligands.",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Lee SJ, McPherron AC. \"Regulation of myostatin activity and muscle growth.\" Proc Natl Acad Sci . 2001;98:9306-9311. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Mendell JR, et al. \"Follistatin gene therapy for sporadic inclusion body myositis.\" Mol Ther . 2017;25:870-879. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Hedger MP, de Kretser DM. \"The activins and their binding proteins - looking back, looking forward.\" Reproduction . 2013;145:R59-R73. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises). Saturation Tracking Half-Life Curves AI Coach 24hr Free Trial Try Free for 24 Hours → Retrieved from \" https://wikipep.org/index.php?title=Follistatin_315&oldid=3910 \" Categories : Peptides Growth Factors Endogenous Peptides Anti-Fibrotic Agents Myostatin Inhibitors Follistatin 315 Add topic",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "Activin Neutralization : Binds activin A with extremely high affinity (Kd ~50-100 pM) → irreversible complex → prevents activin receptor binding → suppresses FSH and catabolic signaling Myostatin Inhibition : Binds and neutralizes myostatin (GDF-8) → removes \"brake\" on muscle growth → muscle hypertrophy GDF-11 Inhibition : Sequesters GDF-11 → reduced anti-proliferative signaling (controversial aging target) BMP Modulation : Binds BMP-2, BMP-4, BMP-6, BMP-7 with moderate affinity → tissue-specific effects Muscle Hypertrophy : Follistatin overexpression → dramatic skeletal muscle hypertrophy (up to 2-3x in animal models) via myostatin/activin blockade Anti-Fibrotic : Reduces TGF-β superfamily-driven fibrosis by neutralizing activin A and BMP signaling in fibrotic tissues Metabolic Effects : Improves insulin sensitivity; promotes brown/beige adipose tissue; reduces hepatic steatosis Reproductive Regulation : Modulates FSH secretion by neutralizing activin at the pituitary level",
