        "lastReviewed": "Not stated",
        "summary": "FOXO4-DRI (FOXO4 D-Retro-Inverso) is the most researched peptide senolytic - a compound that selectively induces apoptosis in senescent cells by blocking the FOXO4-p53 pro-survival interaction. Senescent cells are cells that have permanently stopped dividing but remain metabolically active, secreting pro-inflammatory SASP (Senescence-Associated Secretory Phenotype) compounds including IL-6, TNF-alpha, and matrix metalloproteinases that accelerate aging in surrounding tissue. FOXO4-DRI disrupts the FOXO4-p53 complex specifically in senescent cells (which upregulate FOXO4 to resist apoptosis), restoring p53's pro-apoptotic function and triggering selective senescent cell death while leaving healthy cells intact. The landmark 2017 Nature paper by Baar et al. demonstrated measurable rejuvenation phenotypes in naturally aged mice following treatment. A 2025 Nature Communications study confirmed the mechanism at atomic resolution.",
