        "summary": "09 How This Works FOXO4-DRI is a synthetic peptide that selectively targets senescent cells by blocking the FOXO4-p53 protein interaction [1] [2] . In normal cells, FOXO4 binds to p53 and sequesters it in the nucleus. In senescent cells, disrupting this interaction causes p53 to translocate to the mitochondria, triggering apoptotic cell death specifically in aged, dysfunctional cells while sparing healthy ones [1] . Animal studies have demonstrated that FOXO4-DRI can reduce senescent cell burden, improve tissue function, and mitigate age-related pathologies [3] [4] [5] . The peptide’s D-retro-inverso configuration enhances its stability and resistance to proteolytic degradation [2] .",
