        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Gallium-68 DOTATATE Chemical name ⁶⁸Ga-DOTA-Tyr³-Octreotate Molecular formula C₆₅H₉₂⁶⁸GaN₁₄O₂₆S₂ Molecular weight ~1,545 Da (with ⁶⁸Ga chelated) CAS number 1314294-98-6 Sequence D-Phe-Cys-Tyr-D-Trp-Lys-Thr-Cys-Thr (DOTA-chelated) Length 8 amino acids (somatostatin analog) + DOTA chelator Source Synthetic radiopharmaceutical Half-life 68 minutes (⁶⁸Ga physical half-life) Targets Somatostatin receptor subtype 2 (SSTR2) Bioavailability Intravenous administration (100%) Legal status FDA-approved (2018, NETSPOT); EMA-approved Gallium-68 DOTATATE (trade name NETSPOT , also referred to as ⁶⁸Ga-DOTATATE ) is an FDA-approved positron emission tomography (PET) radiopharmaceutical used for the diagnostic imaging of somatostatin receptor-positive neuroendocrine tumors (NETs) .",
