        "mechanism": "GHK-Cu exerts its biological effects through multiple mechanisms, with its gene-regulatory activity being particularly significant: Gene Expression ModulationGHK-Cu acts as a biological signal that can modulate the expression of approximately 31% of human genes. It tends to reset gene expression toward a more youthful, regenerative pattern. Key affected pathways include those involved in: - Antioxidant and anti-inflammatory responses - Tissue remodelling and repair - DNA repair mechanisms - Stem cell support Collagen Synthesis StimulationThe peptide significantly enhances the production of collagen types I, III, and IV by fibroblasts. This increased collagen production is fundamental to wound healing and skin structural integrity. GHK-Cu also promotes the synthesis of other matrix proteins including decorin and elastin. Angiogenesis PromotionGHK-Cu stimulates the formation of new blood vessels, enhancing blood supply to healing tissues. This improved vascularisation supports nutrient delivery and waste removal essential for tissue repair.",
