        "evidence": "Most users start a Klow protocol for one of four reasons: a soft tissue injury that isn't resolving, visibly aging skin, an inflamed gut, or all three at once. The Klow peptide benefits below are what people consistently report across 8 to 12 week protocols, organized by what changes first. Faster soft tissue repair (weeks 2 to 4): BPC-157 and TB-500 together accelerate tendon, ligament, and muscle healing. This is the single most reported Klow peptide benefit, especially for nagging shoulder, knee, and Achilles issues. Visible skin glow and elasticity (weeks 3 to 6): GHK-Cu drives collagen synthesis and is where the \"glow\" in Klow comes from. Skin tone evens out, fine lines soften, and texture improves within the first 6 weeks. Calmer gut and lower systemic inflammation (weeks 1 to 3): KPV and BPC-157 both modulate gut inflammation and NF-kB signaling. Bloating and food sensitivity often improve before the structural healing benefits arrive.",
