        "mechanism": "GHRP-2 primarily works through the ghrelin receptor : GHS-R ActivationGHRP-2 binds to and activates the growth hormone secretagogue receptor (GHS-R, ghrelin receptor) on pituitary somatotroph cells. This triggers intracellular calcium release and subsequent GH secretion. Hypothalamic EffectsGHRP-2 also acts at the hypothalamic level, stimulating GHRH release and potentially inhibiting somatostatin. These central effects contribute to its GH-releasing action. Cortisol and Prolactin EffectsUnlike the more selective Ipamorelin, GHRP-2 also stimulates cortisol and prolactin release. These effects are generally modest but distinguish GHRP-2 from more selective alternatives. Appetite StimulationThrough ghrelin receptor activation, GHRP-2 can stimulate appetite. This effect is less pronounced than with GHRP-6 but still notable. Synergy with GHRHGHRP-2 works synergistically with GHRH or GHRH analogues. The combination produces greater GH release than additive effects would predict, as the peptides work through complementary receptor systems.",
