        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17T07:42:57+00:00",
        "summary": "09 How This Works GHRP-2 is a synthetic growth hormone secretagogue that binds to and activates ghrelin (GH secretagogue) receptors [1] . This activation triggers potent, pulsatile release of growth hormone from the pituitary gland in a dose-dependent manner [4] . Clinical studies in GH-deficient children demonstrated meaningful GH increases even at low doses (0.3-3.0 mcg/kg), with escalating doses over several months showing sustained efficacy [2] . In healthy adults, doses of 100 mcg SC daily produce acute GH stimulation [3] , while routine protocols typically maintain 100-300 mcg/day to balance efficacy with receptor sensitivity. The peptide has been well tolerated in clinical trials with no significant adverse effects or toxicity reported at these dosage ranges [2] .",
