        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia GHRP-2 Chemical name Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide-2 Molecular formula C45H55N9O6 Molecular weight 817.97 g/mol CAS number 158861-67-7 Sequence D-Ala-D-2-Nal-Ala-Trp-D-Phe-Lys-NH₂ Length 6 amino acids Source Synthetic growth hormone secretagogue Half-life 15-30 minutes Targets Ghrelin receptor (GHS-R1a) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Research compound only GHRP-2 (Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide-2), also known as Pralmorelin, is a synthetic hexapeptide that belongs to the family of growth hormone secretagogues (GHS). Developed in the 1980s and 1990s as part of pharmaceutical research into alternatives to direct growth hormone therapy, GHRP-2 stimulates the body's natural release of growth hormone by mimicking the action of ghrelin, the \"hunger hormone.\" It represents a middle ground among GHRPs, offering potent growth hormone stimulation with moderate appetite effects.",
