        "sourceId": "pep-university",
        "url": "https://pepuniversity.com/peptide-codex.php#ghrp-2",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "GHRP-2 (also known as pralmorelin or KP-102) is a second-generation synthetic hexapeptide Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide and the most scientifically validated GHRP in this database. It is the only GHRP to have achieved any regulatory approval in the world - approved in Japan as pralmorelin for clinical diagnosis of growth hormone deficiency (the GHRP-2 stimulation test), providing a level of formal human pharmacokinetic and safety data uncommon among research peptides. GHRP-2 activates GHS-R1a (the ghrelin receptor) on anterior pituitary somatotrophs, triggering rapid, dose-dependent GH release typically within 15-30 minutes of injection. Its unique D-beta-naphthylalanine (D-BNal) residue at position 2 produces slightly different receptor binding kinetics than GHRP-6, resulting in a pharmacological profile that sits precisely between GHRP-6's non-selective broad stimulation and ipamorelin's highly selective clean profile.",
