        "mechanism": "GHRP-6 works primarily through the ghrelin receptor : GHS-R ActivationGHRP-6 binds to and activates the growth hormone secretagogue receptor (GHS-R), triggering GH release from pituitary somatotrophs. This is the same receptor that responds to endogenous ghrelin. Potent Appetite StimulationGHRP-6's activation of ghrelin receptors in the hypothalamus produces significant appetite stimulation-often described as intense hunger. This is the most pronounced appetite effect among common GHRPs. Effects on Other HormonesGHRP-6 also modestly stimulates cortisol, prolactin, and ACTH release, similar to GHRP-2 but somewhat less pronounced. Cardioprotective EffectsResearch has demonstrated that GHRP-6 can protect heart tissue from ischemic injury through mechanisms that may be partly independent of GH release. These cardioprotective effects are an active area of research. Synergy with GHRHLike other GHRPs, GHRP-6 works synergistically with GHRH and GHRH analogues. The combination produces greater GH release than either alone.",
