        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia GHRP-6 Chemical name Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide-6 Molecular formula C46H56N12O6 Molecular weight 873.03 g/mol CAS number 87616-84-0 Sequence His-D-Trp-Ala-Trp-D-Phe-Lys-NH₂ Length 6 amino acids Source Synthetic growth hormone secretagogue Half-life 15-30 minutes Targets Ghrelin receptor (GHS-R1a) Bioavailability Subcutaneous, oral, intranasal Legal status Research compound only GHRP-6 (Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide-6), also known as Growth Hormone Releasing Hexapeptide, is a synthetic hexapeptide that was the first highly potent member of the growth hormone secretagogue family. Developed in the 1980s, GHRP-6 became the foundation for understanding growth hormone releasing peptides and their mechanisms of action. It is particularly notable for its dual effects: potent growth hormone stimulation and significant appetite enhancement through ghrelin receptor activation.",
