        "summary": "GHRP-6 is the original first-generation synthetic Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide - the foundational compound of the entire GHRP class. Developed in the 1980s, it is a hexapeptide that activates GHS-R1a (ghrelin receptor) on pituitary somatotrophs to trigger pulsatile GH release, but unlike its successors, it activates GHS-R1a with minimal selectivity. The receptor is expressed throughout the body - in the pituitary, hypothalamus, adrenal glands, stomach, and CNS appetite centers - and GHRP-6 hits all of these targets simultaneously. The result is a compound with the strongest appetite stimulation of any GHRP (mediated centrally via NPY/AgRP pathways in the hypothalamus), significant cortisol and prolactin elevation, and robust GH release. In terms of raw GH pulse amplitude at equivalent doses, GHRP-6 produces the largest pulses of any GHRP in this database - but with the least favorable hormonal collateral.",
        "evidence": "Peptide University labels its records as aggregated from empirical research and anecdotal community data. This record is retained as supplied and is not upgraded to clinical evidence.",
