        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Glucagon Chemical name Glucagon Molecular formula C₁₅₃H₂₂₅N₄₃O₄₉S Molecular weight 3482.75 g/mol CAS number 16941-32-5 Sequence HSQGTFTSDYSKYLDSRRAQDFVQWLMNT Length 29 amino acids Source Pancreatic alpha cells (endogenous) / Recombinant Half-life 8-18 minutes Targets Glucagon receptor (GCGR) Bioavailability 100% (injection) Legal status FDA Approved Glucagon is a 29-amino acid peptide hormone produced by the alpha cells of the pancreatic islets of Langerhans. It serves as the primary counterregulatory hormone to insulin, playing a critical role in glucose homeostasis by stimulating hepatic glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis to raise blood glucose levels. Glucagon is FDA-approved as an emergency treatment for severe hypoglycemia and as a diagnostic aid for radiographic examination of the GI tract.",
