        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Glutathione Chemical name γ-L-Glutamyl-L-cysteinylglycine Molecular formula C₁₀H₁₇N₃O₆S Molecular weight 307.32 g/mol CAS number 70-18-8 Sequence Glu-Cys-Gly (γ-peptide bond) Length 3 amino acids (tripeptide) Source Endogenous/Synthetic Half-life 10-15 minutes (IV), 90 minutes (intracellular) Targets Multiple cellular processes Bioavailability IV, IM, nebulized, liposomal oral Legal status Supplement/pharmaceutical Glutathione (GSH) is the body's master antioxidant and most abundant intracellular thiol, a tripeptide composed of glutamate, cysteine, and glycine that plays critical roles in detoxification, immune function, and cellular protection. Present in virtually every cell of the body at millimolar concentrations, glutathione exists in both reduced (GSH) and oxidized (GSSG) forms, with the GSH/GSSG ratio serving as a major indicator of cellular oxidative stress and overall health status.",
