        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Gonadorelin Chemical name Gonadotropin-Releasing Hormone Molecular formula C55H75N17O13 Molecular weight 1182.29 g/mol CAS number 33515-09-2 Sequence pGlu-His-Trp-Ser-Tyr-Gly-Leu-Arg-Pro-Gly-NH₂ Length 10 amino acids Source Synthetic GnRH analog Half-life 2-10 minutes (distribution), 10-40 minutes (terminal) Targets GnRH receptor Bioavailability Intravenous, subcutaneous, intranasal Legal status Prescription medication (FDA approved) Gonadorelin is a synthetic decapeptide that is bioidentical to naturally occurring gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH), also known as luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone (LHRH). This crucial neuropeptide hormone is produced by the hypothalamus and serves as the master regulator of the hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal (HPG) axis.",
