        "summary": "Gotratix is a Khavinson cytomedin - peptide complex A-18 - extracted from skeletal muscle tissue of young animals, developed at the St. Petersburg Institute of Bioregulation and Gerontology as the dedicated muscle bioregulator of the Khavinson framework. It works at the transcriptional level inside myocytes (muscle fibers) and satellite cells (the stem cells that regenerate muscle), normalizing the gene expression programs governing myosin and actin synthesis, mitochondrial biogenesis, oxidative stress resistance, and the activation of MyoD and myogenin - the master regulators of muscle cell identity and repair. In plain terms, Gotratix signals aging muscle cells to restore the protein synthesis capacity, energy efficiency, and regenerative responsiveness they had in youth - independent of any hormonal signal. Gotratix has been studied in athletes, elderly subjects with sarcopenia, and post-surgical muscle recovery populations.",
