        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia HD-5 Chemical name Human Defensin-5 (α-Defensin-5; HD-5; DEFA5) Molecular formula C₁₅₇H₂₄₅N₄₇O₄₇S₆ Molecular weight 3582.3 g/mol CAS number 145090-76-0 Sequence ATCYCRTGRCATRESLSGVCEISGRLYRLCCR (32 aa; 3 disulfide bonds; Paneth cell-specific) Length 32 amino acids (the primary alpha-defensin of the small intestinal Paneth cells) Source Endogenous (Paneth cells at the base of small intestinal crypts; constitutive secretion + microbial stimulation) Half-life Highly stable in intestinal lumen (disulfide-stabilized; resistant to intestinal proteases including trypsin) Targets Microbial membranes → pore formation → killing of intestinal bacteria; also binds bacterial toxins and modulates microbiome composition Bioavailability Secreted directly into intestinal crypt lumen; not absorbed systemically Legal status Research compound (endogenous enteric antimicrobial peptide) HD-5 (Human Defensin-5, α-Defensin-5) is the primary antimicrobial peptide",
