        "sourceId": "pep-university",
        "url": "https://pepuniversity.com/peptide-codex.php#hexarelin",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Hexarelin (also known as examorelin) is the most potent GHRP ever synthesized - a hexapeptide that produces the largest acute GH pulses of any compound in the GHRP class, estimated to generate GH release 2-3 times greater than native GHRH alone at equivalent molar doses. It activates GHS-R1a (the ghrelin receptor) on pituitary somatotrophs with particularly high affinity, simultaneously suppressing hypothalamic somatostatin (the GH-inhibiting hormone) to amplify the net GH output further. Unlike ipamorelin or GHRP-2, hexarelin has no selectivity for the GH response over other GHS-R1a-mediated effects - it elevates cortisol and prolactin significantly with every injection, placing it in the same non-selective category as GHRP-6, but with even greater potency across all pathways.",
