        "summary": "Somatropin is recombinant human growth hormone (rhGH) -- a bioidentical, 191-amino-acid copy of the growth hormone naturally secreted by the anterior pituitary. It is FDA-approved under multiple brand names for a specific list of growth-disorder and deficiency indications, and separately (as Serostim) for HIV-associated wasting. Unlike the GH secretagogues elsewhere in this encyclopedia (e.g., ipamorelin, CJC-1295, GHRP-6), somatropin supplies growth hormone directly rather than stimulating the pituitary to release its own. Somatropin is produced via recombinant DNA technology (typically in E. coli or mammalian expression systems) and is structurally identical to the major isoform of endogenous human growth hormone: a 191-amino-acid, single-chain polypeptide with four cysteine residues forming two intrachain disulfide bonds.",
        "evidence": "Extensive decades-long clinical evidence base supporting FDA-approved indications (pediatric growth disorders, adult GHD, HIV-associated wasting). Off-label use for anti-aging, general athletic performance, or body-composition enhancement in GH-sufficient adults is far more common than approved use but has a substantially thinner and more mixed evidence base, and is not an FDA-approved indication.",
