          "Myalgia (muscle pain) - GH-related; typically transient.",
          "Carpal tunnel syndrome - GH-mediated median nerve compression from fluid retention; more common in adults; may require dose reduction or discontinuation.",
          "Paresthesia (tingling/numbness) - in hands and feet; from GH-related fluid pressure on peripheral nerves.",
          "Decreased insulin sensitivity - progressive with dose and duration; the primary metabolic adverse effect of sustained exogenous GH; monitor fasting glucose.",
          "Elevated fasting blood glucose - direct consequence of GH-induced insulin resistance.",
          "Peripheral swelling (hands, feet, face) - edema, particularly in the first weeks.",
          "Headache - vasodilation and fluid shifts.",
          "Benign intracranial hypertension - rare; typically in pediatric patients; presents as headache, visual changes, nausea; resolves with dose reduction."
