        "summary": "A fragment of human growth hormone corresponding to amino acids 176-191, researched specifically for its fat-metabolising properties.",
        "evidence": "Animal/cell evidence only Not a licensed UK medicine. C-terminal fragment of growth hormone marketed for selective fat loss. Conceptually distinct from full HGH but still captured by WADA growth-factor rules. Human evidence is weak. Human evidence grade D, Animal/cell evidence only. Citation quality grade C, Limited human evidence.",
