        "mechanism": "HGH Fragment 176-191 works through mechanisms distinct from full growth hormone: Lipolysis StimulationThe fragment stimulates the breakdown of triglycerides stored in adipose tissue, releasing fatty acids into the bloodstream for use as energy. This lipolytic effect occurs through activation of hormone-sensitive lipase in fat cells. Lipogenesis InhibitionResearch suggests the fragment inhibits the formation of new fat from dietary carbohydrates and other substrates, potentially reducing fat storage. Selective Fat ActionUnlike full growth hormone, the fragment appears to act primarily on adipose tissue without significant effects on muscle, bone, or other tissues that would respond to complete hGH. IGF-1 IndependenceHGH Fragment 176-191 does not appear to stimulate IGF-1 production, distinguishing its effects from those of full growth hormone and potentially reducing associated risks. Glucose NeutralityStudies suggest the fragment does not significantly affect blood glucose or insulin sensitivity, unlike full growth hormone which can impair glucose metabolism.",
