        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Histatin-5 Chemical name Histatin-5 (Hst-5) Molecular formula C₁₁₉H₁₈₅N₄₃O₃₂ Molecular weight 3036.4 g/mol CAS number 113226-29-8 Sequence DSHAKRHHGYKRKFHEKHHSHRGY (24 aa; histidine-rich; cationic) Length 24 amino acids (histidine-rich peptide; the most potent antifungal peptide in human saliva) Source Endogenous (parotid and submandibular salivary glands; constitutive secretion into oral cavity) Half-life ~1-2 hours in saliva (susceptible to oral proteases; fragments retain partial activity) Targets Fungal mitochondrial membrane → induces ROS, ATP efflux, and non-lytic killing of Candida species; primary defense against oral candidiasis Bioavailability Present in saliva at 15-30 mcg/mL; secreted directly onto oral mucosal surfaces Legal status Research compound (endogenous salivary antifungal peptide) Histatin-5 (Hst-5) is the most potent naturally occurring antifungal peptide in the human body, found exclusively in saliva.",
