        "mechanism": "HMG delivers both gonadotropins needed for reproductive function: Follicular Development FSH component binds to granulosa cell receptors, activating cAMP/PKA signaling to stimulate follicle growth and aromatase expression for estrogen synthesis. Steroidogenesis LH activity stimulates theca cells to produce androgens, which granulosa cells convert to estrogens - the “two-cell, two-gonadotropin” model. Male Fertility In men, FSH supports Sertoli cells for spermatogenesis while LH activity stimulates Leydig cells to produce testosterone - restoring reproductive function. Oocyte Quality Combined FSH/LH activity may improve oocyte and embryo quality compared to FSH alone, particularly in IVF cycles with standard insemination.",
