        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia HMG (Human Menopausal Gonadotropin) Chemical name Menotropin Molecular formula FSH + LH glycoproteins Molecular weight ~30,000 + ~30,000 g/mol CAS number 9002-68-0 Sequence FSH: α + β subunits, LH: α + β subunits Length Multiple chains Source Post-menopausal women's urine Half-life FSH: 24-36 hours, LH: 20 hours Targets FSH and LH/hCG receptors Bioavailability Intramuscular, subcutaneous injection Legal status Prescription only (FDA approved) HMG (Human Menopausal Gonadotropin), also known as menotropin, is a medication containing both follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH) activity, extracted from the urine of postmenopausal women. With a typical 1:1 ratio of FSH to LH activity (75 IU of each per vial), HMG provides comprehensive gonadotropin support that makes it particularly valuable for fertility treatment and maintaining reproductive function in men undergoing testosterone replacement therapy (TRT).",
