        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia IGF-1 (Mecasermin) Chemical name Insulin-like Growth Factor 1; Somatomedin C Molecular formula C₃₃₁H₅₁₂N₉₄O₁₀₁S₇ Molecular weight 7649 g/mol CAS number 67763-96-6 Sequence GPETLCGAELVDALQFVCGDRGFYFNKPTGYGSSSRRAPQTGIVDECCFRSCDLRRLEMYCAPLKPAKSA Length 70 amino acids Source Recombinant (E. coli) / Endogenous human Half-life 10-20 minutes (free); 12-15 hours (bound to IGFBP-3/ALS) Targets IGF-1 receptor (IGF-1R), insulin receptor (low affinity) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection (~100%) Legal status FDA-approved (Increlex) for severe primary IGF-1 deficiency Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 ( IGF-1 ), also known as somatomedin C , is a 70-amino acid polypeptide hormone structurally homologous to proinsulin. It is the primary mediator of the anabolic and growth-promoting effects of growth hormone (GH) and plays a central role in postnatal growth, tissue repair, and metabolic regulation.",
