        "url": "https://pepuniversity.com/peptide-codex.php#igf-1-lr3",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "IGF-1 LR3 (Long R3 Insulin-like Growth Factor-1) is an engineered analog of Insulin-like Growth Factor 1 - the primary downstream mediator of growth hormone's anabolic effects. In normal physiology, GH stimulates the liver to produce IGF-1, which then travels through the bloodstream to promote tissue growth, protein synthesis, and cell survival across multiple organ systems. Standard IGF-1 has a very short functional half-life because it is rapidly bound and inactivated by IGF Binding Proteins (IGFBPs) in the blood. IGF-1 LR3 circumvents this by incorporating two modifications: an arginine substitution at position 3 that dramatically reduces IGFBP binding affinity, and an extended N-terminal sequence (13 amino acid extension) that adds additional binding resistance. The result is an IGF-1 analog with approximately 60-120 times longer functional half-life (20-30 hours) than native IGF-1, which remains active and receptor-available throughout the bloodstream for an extended window.",
