        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia IGF-2 Chemical name Insulin-like Growth Factor 2 Molecular formula C₃₃₇H₅₂₁N₉₁O₁₀₁S₆ Molecular weight 7,471 g/mol CAS number 67763-97-7 Sequence 67 amino acids (mature human IGF-2) Length 67 amino acids Source Endogenous (liver - primarily fetal; many tissues); recombinant Half-life ~15-20 minutes (free); hours when bound to IGFBPs Targets Insulin receptor isoform A (IR-A, primary); IGF-1R (moderate affinity); IGF-2R/M6P (clearance) Bioavailability IV/SC (research) Legal status Research compound (not approved) IGF-2 ( Insulin-like Growth Factor 2 ) is a 67-amino acid peptide hormone structurally related to insulin and IGF-1 that plays a dominant role in fetal growth and development. While IGF-1 is the primary mediator of postnatal growth hormone signaling, IGF-2 is the principal growth factor during embryogenesis, where it drives cell proliferation and organ development through an imprinted gene (expressed primarily from the paternal allele).",
