        "mechanism": "IR-A Activation : Primary mitogenic signaling through insulin receptor isoform A → RAS/MAPK proliferative pathway (distinct from metabolic insulin/IR-B signaling) IGF-1R Activation : Moderate affinity for IGF-1R → PI3K/Akt survival and mTOR/protein synthesis pathways IGF-2R/M6P Receptor : Binds IGF-2R → internalization and lysosomal degradation (clearance, NOT signaling) Fetal Growth : Dominant growth factor during embryonic development; drives placental growth, organ development Genomic Imprinting : Paternally expressed (maternally silenced); IGF-2R maternally expressed → parent-of-origin growth conflict IGFBP Regulation : Circulates bound to IGFBP-1 through IGFBP-6 (IGFBP-6 preferentially binds IGF-2 over IGF-1) Cancer Biology : Re-expression/overexpression drives proliferation in many tumor types via autocrine IR-A signaling Memory and Cognition : IGF-2 in hippocampus critical for memory consolidation and fear extinction",
