        "summary": "Published June 5, 2026 Updated August 28, 2026 Quick Brief The tesamorelin ipamorelin stack pairs an FDA-approved GHRH analog with a selective ghrelin-receptor GHRP that act on two different switches in the growth hormone axis. This guide covers the synergy mechanism, dosing math, what the human trial data actually shows for each peptide, and the safety questions and contraindications behind the blend. Tesamorelin + Ipamorelin Stack: Blend Protocol, Dosing & Synergy (2026) Procurement Embody Compounded Semaglutide Ships from USA Start Semaglutide - $69/mo The tesamorelin ipamorelin stack pairs two growth hormone (GH) peptides that work on completely different switches in the same system. Tesamorelin is a stabilized growth hormone releasing hormone (GHRH) analog that tells the pituitary how much GH to make, while ipamorelin is a selective ghrelin receptor agonist that tells the pituitary when to fire and removes the natural brake (somatostatin) that holds GH back.",
