        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Ipamorelin is a third-generation Growth Hormone Releasing Peptide (GHRP) and the cleanest GH secretagogue available. While all GHRPs work by activating the GHS-R1a (ghrelin receptor) to stimulate pituitary GH release, they differ dramatically in their selectivity. First-generation GHRP-6 and second-generation GHRP-2 both activate GHS-R1a in ways that also elevate cortisol, prolactin, and ACTH alongside GH - producing a messy hormonal picture that limits their long-term utility. Ipamorelin was engineered specifically to resolve this. Its unique pentapeptide structure (Aib-His-D-2-Nal-D-Phe-Lys-NH2) produces potent GHS-R1a activation in pituitary somatotrophs while failing to trigger the cortisol or prolactin responses seen with other GHRPs. This was confirmed in head-to-head pharmacology studies comparing ipamorelin directly against GHRP-2 and GHRP-6 - ipamorelin does not significantly elevate cortisol or ACTH at any studied dose.",
