        "mechanism": "The pathway is clean and well-characterized: Kisspeptin neurons in the hypothalamus (arcuate nucleus and AVPV) fire in pulses These pulses trigger GnRH release into the portal circulation GnRH reaches the anterior pituitary and triggers LH and FSH release LH signals Leydig cells in the testes to produce testosterone (men) or drives follicle development (women) FSH drives spermatogenesis (men) and follicle maturation (women) The pulsatile nature of this system matters. Continuous GnRH stimulation causes receptor downregulation and actually suppresses the axis - which is how GnRH agonists like leuprolide work in prostate cancer treatment. Pulsatile kisspeptin administration, by contrast, stimulates rather than suppresses.",
