        "mechanism": "Acts intracellularly to inhibit pro-inflammatory signaling, including NF-kappaB activation and downstream inflammatory cytokine production. In the gut it is taken up by the peptide transporter PepT1 in intestinal epithelial cells, reducing mucosal inflammation. Retains alpha-MSH anti-inflammatory activity without significant melanocortin pigmentary effects.",
