        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Lanreotide Chemical name Lanreotide acetate Molecular formula C₅₄H₆₉N₁₁O₁₀S₂ Molecular weight 1096.33 g/mol CAS number 108736-35-2 Sequence D-2Nal-Cys-Tyr-D-Trp-Lys-Val-Cys-Thr-NH₂ (cyclic disulfide) Length 8 amino acids (octapeptide) Source Synthetic somatostatin analog Half-life 23-30 days (Autogel depot) Targets Somatostatin receptors (SSTR2, SSTR5) Bioavailability 73-79% (deep SC injection) Legal status FDA Approved (2007) Lanreotide (brand name Somatuline Depot / Somatuline Autogel ) is a long-acting synthetic octapeptide analog of somatostatin approved for the treatment of acromegaly, gastroenteropancreatic neuroendocrine tumors (GEP-NETs), and carcinoid syndrome. Developed by Ipsen, lanreotide is formulated as a supersaturated aqueous solution that forms a drug depot upon deep subcutaneous injection, providing sustained release over 4 weeks.",
