        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Larazotide Chemical name Larazotide acetate (AT-1001 / INN-202) Molecular formula C₃₅H₅₄N₈O₁₁ Molecular weight 762.85 g/mol CAS number 258818-34-7 Sequence Gly-Gly-Val-Leu-Val-Gln-Pro-Gly (octapeptide) Length 8 amino acids Source Synthetic (derived from Vibrio cholerae zonula occludens toxin) Half-life Luminal (acts locally in GI tract - minimal systemic absorption) Targets Zonulin pathway / Tight junction modulation (prevents zonulin-mediated tight junction opening) Bioavailability Oral capsule (acts luminally, not systemically) Legal status Investigational (Phase 3, 9 Meters Biopharma) Larazotide (also known as AT-1001 or INN-202 ) is a first-in-class tight junction regulator being developed for celiac disease and other conditions associated with increased intestinal permeability (\"leaky gut\").",
        "evidence": "Trial Phase Population Key Results Year CeliAction Ph2 Phase 2 Celiac on GFD (n=184) Reduced GI symptoms (GSRS) vs placebo; 0.5 mg optimal 2012 Ph2b (CALY) Phase 2b Celiac on GFD (n=342) Significant reduction in celiac symptom days; 0.5 mg dose 2015 Ph2b gluten challenge Phase 2b Celiac with gluten challenge Prevented symptom exacerbation during controlled gluten exposure 2017 Ph3 (ongoing) Phase 3 Celiac on GFD Primary: symptom reduction (CeD-PRO); 9 Meters Biopharma Ongoing [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Paterson BM, et al. \"The safety, tolerance, pharmacokinetic and pharmacodynamic effects of single doses of AT-1001 in coeliac disease subjects.\" Aliment Pharmacol Ther . 2007;26:757-766. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Kelly CP, et al. \"Larazotide acetate in patients with coeliac disease: a randomised, placebo-controlled Phase 2b trial.\" Lancet Gastroenterol Hepatol . 2015;1:28-37. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Leffler DA, et al. \"Larazotide for celiac disease: rationale and clinical development.\" Expert Rev Gastroenterol Hepatol . 2019.",
        "halfLife": "",
