        "evidence": "Application Route Dose Model Appetite suppression IP/IV 500-2000 μg/kg Mouse GH suppression IV 100-500 μg/kg Rodent In vitro GHS-R1a studies Cell culture 10⁻⁸-10⁻⁵ M GHS-R1a-expressing cells Human biomarker Serum measurement ELISA Clinical cohorts For detailed protocols, see PepDex Wiki . [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Ge X, et al. \"LEAP2 is an endogenous antagonist of the ghrelin receptor.\" Cell Metab . 2018;27(2):461-469. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Mani BK, et al. \"LEAP2 changes with body mass and food intake in humans and mice.\" J Clin Invest . 2019;129(9):3909-3923. ↑ 3.0 3.1 M'Kadmi C, et al. \"N-terminal liver-expressed antimicrobial peptide 2 (LEAP2) region exhibits inverse agonist activity toward the ghrelin receptor.\" J Med Chem . 2019;62:965-973. ↑ Krause A, et al. \"LEAP-1, a novel highly disulfide-bonded human peptide.\" FEBS Lett . 2000;480:147-150. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
