        "mechanism": "Leuphasyl exerts its wrinkle-reducing effects through the enkephalin pathway-a mechanism distinct from the SNARE complex inhibition of Argireline and SNAP-8: Enkephalin Receptor ActivationLeuphasyl's sequence (Tyr-D-Ala-Gly-Phe-Leu) mimics natural enkephalin peptides, allowing it to bind to enkephalin receptors on peripheral nerve terminals in the skin. Mechanism of Action :1. Receptor Binding:Leuphasyl binds to δ-opioid receptors (and possibly μ-opioid receptors) on nerve terminals 2. Calcium Channel Modulation:Receptor activation reduces calcium influx into nerve terminals 3. Reduced Neurotransmitter Release:Lower intracellular calcium decreases acetylcholine vesicle fusion and release 4. Attenuated Muscle Contraction:Less acetylcholine means weaker signals to facial muscles 5. Expression Line Reduction:Reduced muscle contraction intensity allows expression lines to soften Comparison to SNARE-Targeting Peptides:While Argireline and SNAP-8 interfere with the SNARE complex (the fusion machinery), Leuphasyl works upstream by reducing the calcium signal that triggers vesicle fusion.",
