        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Leuprolide Chemical name Leuprorelin acetate Molecular formula C₅₉H₈₄N₁₆O₁₂ Molecular weight 1209.4 g/mol CAS number 53714-56-0 Sequence pGlu-His-Trp-Ser-Tyr-D-Leu-Leu-Arg-Pro-NHEt Length 9 amino acids Source Synthetic GnRH agonist Half-life 3-4 hours (immediate release), 1 month (depot) Targets GnRH receptor Bioavailability Subcutaneous, intramuscular injection Legal status Prescription medication (FDA approved) Leuprolide (also known as leuprorelin) is a synthetic nonapeptide analog of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) that acts as a potent GnRH receptor agonist. First developed in the 1970s and approved by the FDA in 1985, leuprolide has become one of the most widely prescribed medications for conditions requiring suppression of sex hormones.",
