        "url": "https://wikipep.org/wiki/Linaclotide",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Linaclotide Chemical name Linaclotide Molecular formula C₅₉H₉₃N₁₉O₂₅S₆ Molecular weight 1,526.8 Da CAS number 851199-59-2 Sequence CCEYCCNPACTGCY (3 disulfide bonds) Length 14 amino acids Source Synthetic (guanylin analog) Half-life Minimal systemic exposure (acts locally in GI) Targets Guanylate cyclase-C (GC-C) receptor Bioavailability <0.1% (designed for local GI action) Legal status FDA approved (2012, Linzess) Linaclotide (trade name Linzess in US, Constella in EU) is a synthetic 14-amino acid peptide and first-in-class guanylate cyclase-C (GC-C) receptor agonist approved by the FDA in 2012 for the treatment of irritable bowel syndrome with constipation (IBS-C) and chronic idiopathic constipation (CIC) in adults. Developed by Ironwood Pharmaceuticals, linaclotide is structurally related to the endogenous peptides guanylin and uroguanylin that naturally regulate intestinal fluid secretion and transit.",
