        "summary": "Before semaglutide became a household name, there was liraglutide. Approved by the FDA in 2010, it was the drug that proved a once-daily GLP-1 receptor agonist could lower blood sugar, reduce cardiovascular risk, and help people lose weight - all in one molecule.",
        "evidence": "Before semaglutide became a household name, there was liraglutide. Approved by the FDA in 2010, it was the drug that proved a once-daily GLP-1 receptor agonist could lower blood sugar, reduce cardiovascular risk, and help people lose weight - all in one molecule.",
        "halfLife": "",
