          "Gastrointestinal adverse events are the most frequently reported, particularly during dose initiation and titration: Nausea: 28-40% (most common; usually diminishes over time) Diarrhea: 12-21% Constipation: 10-19% Vomiting: 10-16% Abdominal pain/dyspepsia: 5-11% Decreased appetite: 9-14% (often considered beneficial.",
          "Pancreatitis: Cases of acute pancreatitis have been reported with liraglutide and other GLP-1 agonists. In LEADER, pancreatitis occurred in 0.4% of liraglutide versus 0.5% of placebo patients-not statistically different.",
