        "summary": "09 How This Works Livagen’s mechanisms involve peptidase inhibition and epigenetic modulation. The peptide strongly inhibits enkephalin-degrading enzymes (IC50 ≈ 20 μM) in human serum [1] , which may prolong endogenous enkephalin activity. Notably, this occurs without direct opioid receptor binding [1] . In aging cells, Livagen has been shown to induce heterochromatin decondensation and reactivate ribosomal genes [4] . Preclinical studies in rat liver organ cultures demonstrated enhanced cellular structure and regenerative processes [3] , while oral administration in aged rats shifted digestive enzyme activities toward youthful patterns [2] .",
