        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Livagen Chemical name Livagen (KEDA; Lys-Glu-Asp-Ala) Molecular formula C₁₇H₂₉N₅O₈ Molecular weight 447.4 g/mol CAS number 87616-84-0 Sequence Lys-Glu-Asp-Ala (KEDA) Length 4 amino acids (tetrapeptide bioregulator targeting liver tissue) Source Synthetic (Khavinson bioregulator peptide; derived from liver-specific extract analysis) Half-life Minutes (small peptide; rapid hepatic uptake) Targets Hepatocyte gene regulation → liver regeneration, detoxification enzyme expression, albumin synthesis Bioavailability Oral, sublingual, intranasal (tetrapeptides cross cell membranes efficiently) Legal status Research compound / dietary supplement Livagen ( Lys-Glu-Asp-Ala , KEDA ) is a synthetic tetrapeptide bioregulator developed by Professor Vladimir Khavinson, targeting liver tissue. It is the defined short-peptide equivalent of liver-specific extracts, designed to normalize gene expression in hepatocytes during aging and pathological states.",
        "evidence": "DNA Binding : Fluorescence spectroscopy confirmed KEDA tetrapeptide binds to specific DNA sequences, with preferential binding to AT-rich regions in hepatocyte gene promoters Chromatin Effects : Electron microscopy showed Livagen treatment caused decondensation of heterochromatin blocks in hepatocyte nuclei - indicating reactivation of silenced genes Gene Expression : Microarray analysis showed modulation of 42 genes in hepatocytes, including upregulation of albumin, transferrin, and CYP enzymes Animal Models : Improved liver function markers (ALT, AST, albumin) in aging rat models after 10-day Livagen treatment 🧪 Vial Dex The World's Most Advanced Peptide Calculator 100% FREE 💧 Reconstitution Vial + BAC water mixing 📉 Dose & Units Syringe units to draw 🔀 Blend Multi-peptide vial ratios 📚 Stack Protocol Multi-vial dose planning 💨 Nasal Spray Spray bottle concentrations 50+ Peptides 7 Calculators 0 Signup Required Peptide: Livagen Open Free Calculator → [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Khavinson VK, et al.",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "Hepatocyte Gene Regulation : Binds DNA regulatory sequences in liver cells → upregulates genes for albumin synthesis, cytochrome P450 enzymes, and glutathione transferase Chromatin Decondensation : Causes heterochromatin → euchromatin transition in hepatocyte nuclei → increased gene accessibility and transcription Liver Regeneration : Promotes hepatocyte proliferation and regenerative capacity Detoxification Enhancement : Upregulates Phase I (CYP450) and Phase II (glutathione conjugation) detoxification enzymes Anti-Fibrotic : May reduce hepatic stellate cell activation → decreased collagen deposition → anti-fibrotic effect Albumin Synthesis : Restores albumin production in aging hepatocytes → improved protein transport and oncotic pressure",
