        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Maritide Chemical name Maritide (AMG 133, MariTide) Molecular formula Bispecific antibody-peptide conjugate Molecular weight ~220,000 Da CAS number - Sequence Anti-GIPR antibody conjugated to GLP-1 agonist peptides Length Bispecific (antibody + 2 GLP-1 peptides) Source Engineered bispecific Half-life ~3-4 weeks Targets GIP receptor (antagonist) + GLP-1 receptor (agonist) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Phase 3 (Investigational) Maritide ( AMG 133 , also styled MariTide ) is a first-in-class bispecific antibody-peptide conjugate developed by Amgen that combines GIP receptor antagonism with GLP-1 receptor agonism in a single molecule. It consists of a fully human anti-GIPR blocking antibody conjugated to two GLP-1 receptor agonist peptides, creating a unique pharmacological profile: simultaneous activation of GLP-1R and inhibition of GIPR.",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Amgen. \"AMG 133 Phase 1 and Phase 2 data presentations.\" Obesity Week 2023-2024. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Lu SC, et al. \"AMG 133, a novel combination of a GIP receptor antagonist and GLP-1 receptor agonist.\" Diabetes . 2023. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Killion EA, et al. \"Anti-obesity effects of GIPR antagonism alone and in combination with GLP-1R agonism in preclinical models.\" Sci Transl Med . 2020. ↑ Samms RJ, et al. \"How may GIP enhance the therapeutic efficacy of GLP-1?\" Trends Endocrinol Metab . 2020;31(6):410-421. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises). Saturation Tracking Half-Life Curves AI Coach 24hr Free Trial Try Free for 24 Hours → Retrieved from \" https://wikipep.org/index.php?title=Maritide&oldid=3982 \" Categories : Peptides GLP-1 Receptor Agonists GIP Receptor Antagonists Bispecific Antibodies Obesity Treatments Investigational Drugs Maritide Add topic",
