        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Maropitant Chemical name (2S,3S)-2-Benzhydryl-N-(5-tert-butyl-2-methoxybenzyl)quinuclidin-3-amine Molecular formula C₃₂H₃₈N₂O Molecular weight 478.7 Da CAS number 147116-67-4 (citrate: 359875-09-1) Sequence Non-peptide (small molecule NK1 antagonist) Length N/A (small molecule) Source Synthetic Half-life 7-8 hours (dogs); 13-17 hours (cats) Targets Neurokinin-1 (NK1) receptor Bioavailability 24% (oral, dogs); improved with feeding Legal status Veterinary prescription (FDA-approved for dogs/cats) Maropitant (trade name Cerenia , marketed by Zoetis) is a potent and selective neurokinin-1 (NK1) receptor antagonist approved exclusively for veterinary use as an antiemetic in dogs and cats.",
        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 De la Puente-Redondo VA et al. (2007). \"The neurokinin-1 receptor antagonist maropitant citrate (Cerenia) is an efficacious and safe treatment for emesis in dogs.\" J Vet Pharmacol Ther . 30(4):365-73. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Benchaoui HA et al. (2007). \"Efficacy of maropitant for preventing vomiting associated with motion sickness in dogs.\" Vet Rec . 161(13):444-7. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Boscan P et al. (2011). \"Effect of maropitant on the MAC of isoflurane in dogs.\" Vet Anaesth Analg . 38(2):83-9. ↑ Niyom S et al. (2013). \"Effect of maropitant on minimum alveolar concentration of sevoflurane during visceral stimulation in cats.\" Vet Anaesth Analg . P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
