        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Mazdutide Chemical name Mazdutide (IBI362 / LY3305677) Molecular formula Acylated GLP-1/glucagon dual agonist peptide Molecular weight ~4,500 g/mol (estimated) CAS number Not yet assigned publicly Sequence Proprietary GLP-1/GCG dual agonist (C18 fatty acid acylated) Length ~30 amino acids (estimated) Source Synthetic (Innovent Biologics / Eli Lilly) Half-life ~6-7 days (supports weekly dosing) Targets GLP-1 receptor + Glucagon receptor (dual agonist) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Approved (China, 2024); Investigational (global Phase 3) Mazdutide (development codes IBI362 and LY3305677 ) is a once-weekly subcutaneous GLP-1/glucagon receptor dual agonist developed by Innovent Biologics in collaboration with Eli Lilly. Mazdutide was approved in China in 2024 for obesity treatment, making it one of the first GLP-1/glucagon dual agonists to reach market approval.",
        "evidence": "Trial Phase Population Key Results Year GLORY-1 Phase 3 Obesity (China, n=610) −14.4% body weight (9 mg, 48 wks) vs −2.6% placebo 2024 GLORY-2 Phase 3 T2DM + obesity (China) HbA1c −1.5%; weight −11.3% 2024 DREAMS-1 Phase 2 NAFLD/NASH Significant hepatic fat reduction (MRI-PDFF) 2024 Global Phase 3 Phase 3 Obesity (global) Ongoing (multiple doses) Initiated 2024 [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Innovent Biologics. \"Mazdutide Phase 3 GLORY-1 results.\" Presented at ADA. 2024. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Ji L, et al. \"Mazdutide in Chinese adults with obesity: GLORY-1 Phase 3 trial.\" Lancet Diabetes Endocrinol . 2024. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Ambery P, et al. \"Pharmacology of GLP-1/glucagon dual agonists.\" Nat Rev Drug Discov . 2023. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
