        "url": "https://wikipep.org/wiki/Melanotan_1",
        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Melanotan 1 Chemical name Afamelanotide Molecular formula C₇₈H₁₁₁N₂₁O₁₉ Molecular weight 1646.85 g/mol CAS number 75921-69-6 Sequence Ac-Ser-Tyr-Ser-Nle-Glu-His-D-Phe-Arg-Trp-Gly-Lys-Pro-Val-NH₂ Length 13 amino acids Source Synthetic α-MSH analog Half-life 30-60 minutes Targets MC1R (melanocortin-1 receptor) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status FDA approved as Scenesse for EPP Melanotan 1 (MT-1), also known as afamelanotide when used pharmaceutically, is a synthetic analog of alpha-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (α-MSH) that was originally developed at the University of Arizona in the 1980s. Unlike its more controversial cousin Melanotan 2, MT-1 is a more selective melanocortin receptor agonist that primarily targets the MC1R receptor responsible for melanogenesis, resulting in increased melanin production and skin pigmentation without significant effects on libido or appetite.",
        "evidence": "EPP Treatment : FDA-approved for photosensitivity disorder DNA Protection : Reduces UV-induced DNA damage Skin Cancer Prevention : May reduce melanoma risk Sunburn Protection : Increases minimal erythema dose (MED) Vitiligo Treatment : Research for repigmentation therapy Reddit Forums : Discussion on r/Peptides about tanning protocols Bodybuilding Forums : Extensive user experiences Medical Groups : EPP patient support communities Dermatology Research : Photoprotection studies EPP Studies : Significant improvement in sun tolerance Phase III Trials : Led to FDA approval for EPP Photoprotection Research : Increased MED documented Quality of Life : Improved outcomes in EPP patients Melanin Density : 30-40% increase in epidermal melanin Eumelanin/Pheomelanin Ratio : Favorable shift Distribution Pattern : More uniform than UV tanning Cellular Studies : Direct melanocyte stimulation confirmed MED Increase : 47-100% increase in sun tolerance DNA Damage : Reduced cyclobutane pyrimidine dimers Inflammatory Markers : Decreased UV-induced cytokines Long-term Protection : Sustained benefits",
