        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "MK-677 (ibutamoren) is a non-peptide, orally active GH secretagogue - the only compound in this database that stimulates the GH axis without requiring subcutaneous injection. It is a small molecule ghrelin mimetic that binds and activates GHS-R1a (the ghrelin receptor) with high selectivity, producing sustained elevations of both GH and IGF-1 that persist for 24 hours following a single daily dose. Unlike the peptide GHRPs (ipamorelin, GHRP-2, GHRP-6) which produce sharp GH pulses that clear within hours, MK-677's oral bioavailability and long half-life (~24 hours) create a continuous hormonal elevation rather than pulsatile bursts. This means it does not mimic natural GH pulse physiology but instead maintains a steady IGF-1 plateau - with the attendant advantages of consistent anabolic and recovery signaling and the disadvantages of sustained rather than physiologic GH exposure.",
