        "lastReviewed": "Not stated",
        "summary": "MOTS-c (Mitochondrial ORF of the 12S rRNA type-c) is a 16-amino acid peptide uniquely encoded within the mitochondrial genome - one of the few known peptides not originating from nuclear DNA. This gives it a direct and fundamental relationship with mitochondrial metabolic state. Under metabolic stress, MOTS-c translocates from mitochondria to the cell nucleus, where it binds stress-response transcription factors NRF2 and ATF1 to reprogram cellular metabolism. Its primary signaling mechanism activates AMPK (AMP-activated protein kinase) - the same master metabolic switch triggered by intense exercise - which drives glucose uptake, fatty acid oxidation, and mitochondrial biogenesis.",
