        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Myostatin Chemical name Myostatin (Growth/Differentiation Factor 8, GDF-8) Molecular formula C₅₃₂H₈₃₆N₁₄₈O₁₅₆S₈ Molecular weight ~25,000 g/mol (active homodimer) CAS number 272502-12-2 Sequence 109 amino acids per monomer (mature form); TGF-β superfamily Length 109 amino acids (mature monomer) Source Endogenous (skeletal muscle) Half-life ~5-7 minutes Targets ActRIIB / ALK4/ALK5 → Smad2/3 Bioavailability Circulates bound to propeptide and follistatin Legal status Research compound; anti-myostatin therapies in clinical trials Myostatin (also known as GDF-8 , Growth/Differentiation Factor 8 ) is a member of the TGF-β superfamily that functions as the primary negative regulator of skeletal muscle mass. Discovered in 1997 by Se-Jin Lee at Johns Hopkins, myostatin's function was dramatically demonstrated by the phenotype of myostatin-knockout mice - which develop approximately twice the normal muscle mass (\"mighty mice\").",
        "evidence": "Knockout Mice (1997) : Se-Jin Lee demonstrated myostatin-null mice have 2-3x normal muscle mass with hyperplasia and hypertrophy Belgian Blue Cattle : Natural myostatin mutations produce extreme muscling - used commercially in meat production Human Case (2004) : German infant born with myostatin mutation showed visible muscular development; remained healthy and exceptionally strong Sarcopenia : Myostatin levels increase with age; elderly have ~30% higher circulating myostatin than young adults Cancer Cachexia : Tumor-derived factors upregulate myostatin → muscle wasting; anti-myostatin may preserve lean mass Translation Gap : Despite dramatic animal results, human anti-myostatin trials have shown only modest efficacy (2-5% lean mass gain), suggesting compensatory activin signaling 🧪 Vial Dex The World's Most Advanced Peptide Calculator 100% FREE 💧 Reconstitution Vial + BAC water mixing 📉 Dose & Units Syringe units to draw 🔀 Blend Multi-peptide vial ratios 📚 Stack Protocol Multi-vial dose planning 💨 Nasal Spray Spray bottle concentrations 50+ Peptides 7 Calculators 0 Signup",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "ActRIIB Signaling : Myostatin binds activin type IIB receptor (ActRIIB) → recruits ALK4/ALK5 type I receptors → Smad2/3 phosphorylation Myoblast Inhibition : Smad2/3 signaling inhibits MyoD and myogenin transcription factors → blocks myoblast proliferation and differentiation Satellite Cell Quiescence : Maintains muscle satellite (stem) cells in quiescent state, limiting regenerative capacity Protein Degradation : Activates ubiquitin-proteasome pathway via atrogin-1/MAFbx and MuRF1 → accelerated muscle protein breakdown mTOR Suppression : Inhibits Akt/mTOR signaling → reduced protein synthesis in muscle fibers Latent Complex Regulation : Secreted bound to propeptide; further regulated by follistatin, FLRG (FSTL3), GASP-1, and decorin Adipose Cross-Talk : Myostatin also signals in adipose tissue - myostatin inhibition promotes brown adipose differentiation and reduces fat mass Muscle-Bone Interaction : Muscle-derived myostatin influences bone formation; myostatin inhibition increases bone mineral density",
