        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia NAD+ Chemical name Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide Molecular formula C21H27N7O14P2 Molecular weight 663.43 g/mol CAS number 53-84-9 Sequence Not a peptide - Dinucleotide coenzyme Length N/A - Small molecule Source Synthetic or biological extraction Half-life 1-2 hours (IV), varies by route Targets Sirtuins, PARPs, CD38, mitochondria Bioavailability IV, IM, SubQ, intranasal Legal status Supplement/research compound NAD+ (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide) is a critical coenzyme found in all living cells that plays a fundamental role in energy metabolism, DNA repair, gene expression, and cellular signaling. As one of the most important molecules for life, NAD+ serves as a cofactor for over 500 enzymatic reactions and is essential for the function of sirtuins, poly(ADP-ribose) polymerases (PARPs), and other NAD-dependent enzymes.",
