          "Chest tightness or pressure - occurs with rapid injection; a vagal response to the acute NAD+ pulse; not a sign of cardiac event; resolves immediately upon slowing the injection rate.",
          "Nausea - associated with rapid injection or higher loading doses; vagally mediated.",
          "Flushing and sensation of warmth - NAD+ and its metabolites have mild vasodilatory effects; facial and truncal flushing within minutes of injection; typically transient.",
          "Headache - reported in a significant minority of users, particularly with early doses; possibly related to cerebral vasodilation and NAD+ pathway flux.",
          "Dizziness - vasodilation-related; particularly in the first minutes post-injection.",
