        "mechanism": "Octreotide is a synthetic cyclic octapeptide analogue of somatostatin with a substantially longer duration of action than the endogenous hormone. It suppresses secretion of growth hormone and several gastrointestinal and pancreatic hormones. FDA-approved uses include acromegaly and symptomatic control of hormone secretion from metastatic carcinoid tumors and VIPomas. Long-acting depot formulations allow chronic therapy at multi-week dosing intervals.",
