        "mechanism": "OGP and its active fragment OGP(10-14) signal through a Gi-protein-coupled receptor pathway: Gi-Protein Receptor Activation - Binds an unidentified Gi-protein-coupled receptor on osteoblast precursors and stromal cells, triggering intracellular signaling cascades; the specific receptor has not yet been cloned, though pharmacological evidence clearly demonstrates Gi coupling (pertussis toxin-sensitive) RAS-MAPK/ERK Cascade - Gi activation leads to Ras → Raf → MEK → ERK1/2 phosphorylation, the primary proliferative signal driving osteoblast precursor expansion Osteoblast Differentiation - Upregulates master osteogenic transcription factors Runx2/Cbfa1, osterix (Sp7), and downstream targets including alkaline phosphatase (ALP), osteocalcin, and type I collagen - driving committed osteoblast maturation IGF-1 Axis Activation - Stimulates local IGF-1 production in bone tissue, creating an autocrine/paracrine amplification loop for osteoblast proliferation and matrix synthesis TGF-β2 Upregulation - Increases TGF-β2 expression in bone marrow, contributing to stromal cell recruitment and",
