        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Orforglipron (LY3502970) Chemical name Orforglipron; LY3502970; OWL-833 Molecular formula C₄₈H₄₈F₂N₁₀O₅ Molecular weight 882.96 g/mol CAS number 2212020-52-3 Sequence N/A (non-peptide small molecule GLP-1 receptor agonist) Length Non-peptide (small molecule) Source Synthetic Half-life ~29-49 hours (enabling once-daily oral dosing) Targets Glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor (GLP-1R); full agonist Bioavailability Oral (precise bioavailability not disclosed; designed for oral absorption) Legal status Investigational (Phase 3 clinical trials) Orforglipron , known by its development codes LY3502970 and OWL-833 , is an investigational oral non-peptide glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor (GLP-1R) agonist being developed by Eli Lilly for the treatment of type 2 diabetes and obesity.",
        "evidence": "ACHIEVE-1: Phase 3 monotherapy trial in T2D ACHIEVE-2/3/4: Phase 3 combination therapy trials with various background medications ATTAIN-1: Phase 3 obesity trial in adults without diabetes ATTAIN-2: Phase 3 obesity trial in adults with type 2 diabetes Available as chemical reference standard for research Used in GLP-1R binding and signaling assays Tool compound for studying non-peptide GLP-1R activation mechanisms [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] [ 5 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Frias JP, Hsia S, Eyde S, et al. \"Efficacy and safety of oral orforglipron in patients with type 2 diabetes: a multicentre, randomised, dose-response, phase 2 study.\" Lancet . 2023;402(10400):472-483. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Wharton S, Blevins T, Connery L, et al. \"Daily oral GLP-1 receptor agonist orforglipron for adults with obesity.\" New England Journal of Medicine . 2023;389(10):877-888. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Kawai T, Sun B, Yoshino H, et al. \"Structural basis for GLP-1 receptor activation by LY3502970, an orally active nonpeptide agonist.\" Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences . 2020;117(47):29959-29967. ↑ Eli Lilly and Company.",
