          "Mild nausea or digestive changes - as hepatic bile acid synthesis and secretion normalizes, some subjects experience mild digestive changes (altered bile flow, minor bowel habit changes) in the first week; typically transient.",
          "Mild fatigue in first cycle days - hepatocyte metabolic reprogramming imposes a transient energy cost; mild fatigue in days 1-3 is occasionally reported; resolves rapidly.",
          "Injection site mild reaction - standard subcutaneous peptide response.",
          "Potential mild bilirubin fluctuation - as hepatocyte processing of bilirubin normalizes, minor transient changes in serum bilirubin may occur in subjects with pre-existing hepatic synthetic dysfunction.",
          "No serious hepatic adverse events documented in the Khavinson research literature at standard protocol doses - Ovagen's safety profile in NAFLD, chronic hepatitis (compensated), and aging liver disease populations is clean.",
