        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Oxyntomodulin Chemical name Oxyntomodulin (OXM / Glucagon-37) Molecular formula C₁₈₄H₂₈₁N₅₁O₆₁S₁ Molecular weight 4449.7 g/mol CAS number 62340-29-8 Sequence HSQGTFTSDYSKYLDSRRAQDFVQWLMNTKRNRNNIA (37 amino acids - glucagon(1-29) + IP-1 octapeptide extension) Length 37 amino acids Source Endogenous (intestinal L-cells, post-prandial release); synthetic Half-life ~12 minutes (native; DPP-IV and NEP cleavage) Targets GLP-1 receptor (moderate agonist) + Glucagon receptor (weaker agonist) - endogenous dual agonist Bioavailability IV/SC injection (research); engineered analogs in development Legal status Research compound; engineered analogs in clinical trials Oxyntomodulin ( OXM ) is a 37-amino acid peptide hormone produced by intestinal L-cells in response to food intake.",
        "evidence": "Continuous IV infusion (3.1 pmol/kg/min × 4 days): −0.5 kg weight loss SC injection (400 nmol TID × 4 weeks): −2.3 kg weight loss + 9.4% increase in energy expenditure 26% reduction in ad libitum food intake (acute infusion) No compensatory decrease in activity (unlike caloric restriction) [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Wynne K, et al. \"Oxyntomodulin increases energy expenditure and decreases food intake in humans.\" Int J Obes . 2006;30:1729-1736. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Cohen MA, et al. \"Oxyntomodulin suppresses appetite and reduces food intake in humans.\" J Clin Endocrinol Metab . 2003;88:4696-4701. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Baggio LL, Drucker DJ. \"Glucagon-like peptides and oxyntomodulin: biology and clinical potential.\" Nat Rev Drug Discov . 2007;6:349-361. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
