        "summary": "P21 is a tetrapeptide (DAVP sequence) derived from the C-terminal region of CNTF (Ciliary Neurotrophic Factor) that stimulates hippocampal neurogenesis - the formation of new neurons in the brain's primary memory and spatial navigation center - without triggering CNTF's adverse off-target effects including severe weight loss, inflammation, cachexia, and broad systemic toxicity that limit CNTF's research utility. P21 was developed specifically to isolate CNTF's neuroprotective and neurogenic activity in a small, BBB-penetrant peptide. Its mechanisms include stimulation of BDNF (Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor) expression, reduction of tau phosphorylation (a hallmark of Alzheimer's pathology and tauopathies), inhibition of CNTF's negative feedback through SOCS proteins, and direct promotion of neural progenitor cell differentiation in the hippocampal dentate gyrus. In Alzheimer's disease animal models, P21 increased brain volume and hippocampal cell counts.",
