        "mechanism": "Pancreastatin exerts its metabolic effects through multiple pathways: Insulin Secretion Inhibition - Directly acts on pancreatic β-cells to suppress glucose-stimulated insulin release; mechanism involves inhibition of adenylyl cyclase, reducing intracellular cAMP and calcium mobilization required for insulin exocytosis Hepatic Glycogenolysis - Stimulates glycogen phosphorylase activity in hepatocytes, promoting glucose-6-phosphate production and hepatic glucose output, contributing to hyperglycemia Adipocyte Insulin Resistance - Inhibits insulin-stimulated glucose uptake (GLUT4 translocation) and lipogenesis in adipose tissue, reducing peripheral glucose disposal Counter-Regulatory to Catestatin - PST and catestatin (another CgA-derived peptide) exert opposing effects on glucose homeostasis: PST is diabetogenic while catestatin is insulin-sensitizing, creating a built-in regulatory balance within the CgA processing cascade Nitric Oxide Inhibition - Reduces endothelial nitric oxide synthase (eNOS) activity, contributing to endothelial dysfunction and potentially linking metabolic",
