        "evidence": "Trial Phase Indication Key Results Year B2305 (Cushing's) Phase 3 Cushing's disease (n=162) UFC normalization: 26% (0.6 mg BID) and 31% (0.9 mg BID) at 6 months 2012 PAOLA (Acromegaly) Phase 3 Acromegaly (inadequate octreotide/lanreotide) GH<2.5 + IGF-1 normal: 15-20% (better than continued SSA) 2014 Phase 3 extension Long-term Cushing's and acromegaly Sustained efficacy at 2-3 years; safety manageable with anti-diabetic therapy 2016 [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Colao A, et al. \"Pasireotide B2305 Study Group: A 12-month Phase 3 study of pasireotide in Cushing's disease.\" N Engl J Med . 2012;366:914-924. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Gadelha MR, et al. \"Pasireotide versus continued treatment with octreotide or lanreotide in acromegaly (PAOLA).\" J Clin Endocrinol Metab . 2014;99:791-799. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Lacroix A, et al. \"Cushing's syndrome - medical therapy update.\" Lancet Diabetes Endocrinol . 2015;3:569-576. P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring.",
        "halfLife": "",
