        "mechanism": "Multi-SSTR Agonism : Activates SSTR1, SSTR2, SSTR3, and SSTR5 → Gi coupling → inhibits adenylyl cyclase → reduced cAMP → decreased hormone secretion SSTR5 Selectivity : 40x greater affinity for SSTR5 than octreotide - critical for Cushing's disease (corticotroph adenomas express mainly SSTR5) ACTH Suppression : Inhibits ACTH secretion from corticotroph adenomas → reduces cortisol production (Cushing's disease) GH/IGF-1 Suppression : Inhibits GH secretion from somatotroph adenomas → normalizes IGF-1 (acromegaly) Antisecretory : Suppresses TSH, GH, insulin, glucagon, gastrin, VIP, and other peptide hormones Antiproliferative : Inhibits pituitary tumor cell proliferation via SSTR2/SSTR5-mediated cell cycle arrest Hyperglycemia : SSTR5 agonism strongly inhibits insulin secretion from pancreatic beta cells → significant hyperglycemia (main dose-limiting toxicity)",
