        "summary": "Peg-MGF (Pegylated Mechano Growth Factor) is the extended half-life version of MGF, produced by attaching polyethylene glycol (PEG) chains to the MGF peptide backbone - the same pegylation technology used to extend the half-life of pharmaceutical biologics. In its native form, MGF is degraded within 5-7 minutes in the bloodstream by the rapid cleavage of its C-terminal E-domain. Pegylation shields the peptide from enzymatic degradation, extending the functional half-life to approximately 48 hours. This single pharmacokinetic change transforms MGF from a locally acting, immediately post-workout tool into a systemically distributed, subcutaneously injectable compound that circulates and activates satellite cells throughout the body - not just in the injected muscle. The extended half-life fundamentally changes the administration logic.",
