        "evidence": "[ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Nickel JC et al. (2015). \"Pentosan polysulfate sodium therapy for interstitial cystitis.\" J Urol . 193(3):857-62. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Jain N et al. (2019). \"Pigmentary maculopathy associated with chronic exposure to pentosan polysulfate sodium.\" Ophthalmology . 126(12):1575-83. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Elmiron Prescribing Information (2020 update). Janssen Pharmaceuticals. ↑ Ghosh P, Smith M (2002). \"Pentosan polysulfate: a novel concept for the treatment of osteoarthritis.\" Semin Arthritis Rheum . P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises). Saturation Tracking Half-Life Curves AI Coach 24hr Free Trial Try Free for 24 Hours → Retrieved from \" https://wikipep.org/index.php?title=Pentosan_Polysulfate&oldid=4037 \" Categories : Peptides Glycosaminoglycan Analogs Approved Drugs Urology Semi-synthetic Compounds Pentosan Polysulfate Add topic",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "PPS exerts its therapeutic effects through multiple pathways: GAG Layer Restoration - PPS structurally mimics endogenous glycosaminoglycans (heparan sulfate, chondroitin sulfate) and binds to the urothelial surface, restoring the deficient mucin/GAG protective barrier in interstitial cystitis Anti-inflammatory Activity - Inhibits complement activation (C3/C5), reduces mast cell degranulation, and suppresses histamine release in the bladder wall, decreasing neurogenic inflammation Heparin-like Anticoagulant Activity - Weak anticoagulant (1/15 the potency of heparin); inhibits thrombin and Factor Xa; anti-thrombotic properties contribute to microvascular flow improvement Growth Factor Modulation - Binds and modulates FGF-2 (basic FGF) and HGF signaling; in cartilage, promotes chondrocyte proliferation and matrix synthesis; anti-angiogenic effects via VEGF pathway modulation Anti-fibrotic Effects - Reduces TGF-β-mediated fibrosis in multiple tissue models; inhibits collagen deposition and myofibroblast differentiation Complement Inhibition - Blocks classical and alternative complement",
