        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Pinealon Chemical name Pinealon (EDR; Glu-Asp-Arg) Molecular formula C₁₄H₂₃N₅O₈ Molecular weight 405.4 g/mol CAS number 105184-37-0 Sequence Glu-Asp-Arg (EDR) Length 3 amino acids (tripeptide bioregulator derived from pineal gland extracts) Source Synthetic (Khavinson bioregulator peptide; originally isolated from pineal gland extract Epithalamin) Half-life Minutes (small peptide; rapid tissue uptake and intracellular accumulation) Targets Pineal gland gene regulation → melatonin synthesis enzymes (AANAT, HIOMT); may interact directly with DNA regulatory sequences Bioavailability Oral, sublingual, intranasal (small peptides can cross cell membranes and potentially BBB) Legal status Research compound / dietary supplement (not FDA-approved; available as bioregulator supplement) Pinealon ( Glu-Asp-Arg , EDR ) is a synthetic tripeptide bioregulator developed by Professor Vladimir Khavinson at the Saint Petersburg Institute of Bioregulation and",
