        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia PL-8177 Chemical name PL-8177 (Melanocortin MC1R Agonist) Molecular formula Modified cyclic peptide Molecular weight ~1,100 Da (estimated) CAS number N/A (investigational) Sequence Modified cyclic α-MSH analog (proprietary) Length 8 amino acids (cyclic, modified) Source Synthetic Half-life 2-6 hours (estimated) Targets Melanocortin MC1 receptor (MC1R) Bioavailability Rectal/topical (targeted GI delivery) Legal status Investigational (Phase 2) PL-8177 is a synthetic selective melanocortin MC1 receptor (MC1R) agonist developed by Palatin Technologies for the treatment of inflammatory bowel disease (IBD) , specifically ulcerative colitis (UC) . It represents a first-in-class approach to treating GI inflammation through targeted activation of the melanocortin system - a family of anti-inflammatory peptide pathways that have been extensively validated in preclinical models but have not yet yielded an IBD-approved therapy.",
        "evidence": "Trial Phase Design Population Key Endpoints NCT04114006 Phase 2 Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled Mild-to-moderate left-sided UC Clinical remission, endoscopic improvement, mucosal healing Route - Rectal suppository / enema - Local colonic delivery Duration - 8-12 weeks treatment - Efficacy and safety assessment [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] [ 4 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Danese S et al. (2019). \"Melanocortin system in inflammatory bowel disease: a novel therapeutic target.\" Gut . ↑ 2.0 2.1 Palatin Technologies (2021). \"PL-8177 Phase 2 Clinical Trial in Ulcerative Colitis.\" ClinicalTrials.gov NCT04114006. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Getting SJ et al. (2003). \"Melanocortin peptide therapy for the treatment of arthritic pathologies.\" Sci World J . ↑ Maaser C et al. (2006). \"Role of the melanocortin system in inflammation.\" Ann N Y Acad Sci . P Pep Dex Track saturation levels, half-life decay curves, and injection schedules for 50+ peptides. AI coaching, blood work correlation, and side effect monitoring. Includes MacroDex (4.39M foods) & FitDex (1,356 exercises).",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "PL-8177 activates the melanocortin anti-inflammatory cascade through MC1R: MC1R Selective Activation - Binds and activates MC1R on immune cells (macrophages, neutrophils, dendritic cells) and intestinal epithelial cells with >1000-fold selectivity over other melanocortin receptors cAMP/PKA Signaling - MC1R activation increases intracellular cAMP through Gαs coupling, activating protein kinase A (PKA), which phosphorylates and inhibits NF-κB nuclear translocation NF-κB Suppression - Inhibits the master inflammatory transcription factor NF-κB, reducing expression of TNF-α, IL-1β, IL-6, IL-8, and other pro-inflammatory cytokines Neutrophil Chemotaxis Inhibition - Reduces neutrophil migration to sites of inflammation by downregulating adhesion molecules (ICAM-1, E-selectin) and chemoattractant receptors Macrophage Polarization - Shifts macrophage phenotype from pro-inflammatory M1 toward pro-resolving M2, promoting tissue repair and resolution of inflammation Epithelial Barrier Protection - Enhances tight junction protein expression (claudins, occludins) in intestinal epithelium,",
        "limitations": [],
        "safety": [
          "Rectal administration: Expected to minimize systemic exposure and off-target effects MC1R selectivity advantage: Avoids MC4R-mediated appetite suppression, MC3R-mediated metabolic effects, and MC4R-mediated cardiovascular effects (hypertension, sexual arousal) Theoretical skin effects: MC1R activation on melanocytes."
        ],
