        "summary": "Prostamax is a synthetic tetrapeptide (Lys-Glu-Asp-Trp) Khavinson bioregulator derived from prostate gland tissue polypeptide extracts - identified as the bioactive core sequence responsible for the prostate epithelial cell regulatory, anti-inflammatory, and tissue-normalizing activity of the native prostatic extract. The prostate is a walnut-sized glandular organ in the male pelvis that produces the fluid components of semen, including citric acid, zinc, proteolytic enzymes (PSA/kallikrein-3), and seminal plasma proteins that constitute approximately 30% of ejaculate volume. The glandular and stromal architecture of the prostate is regulated by a complex androgen-dependent and growth factor-dependent tissue homeostasis involving prostatic epithelial cells, prostatic stromal fibroblasts, and smooth muscle cells.",
