        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia PT-141 Chemical name Bremelanotide Molecular formula C50H68N14O10 Molecular weight 1025.2 g/mol CAS number 189691-06-3 Sequence Ac-Nle-cyclo[Asp-His-D-Phe-Arg-Trp-Lys]-OH Length 7 amino acids (cyclic) Source Synthetic melanocortin receptor agonist Half-life 2.7 hours Targets Melanocortin receptors (MC1R, MC3R, MC4R) Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection, intranasal Legal status FDA approved as Vyleesi (2019) PT-141 (also known as Bremelanotide and marketed as Vyleesi ) is a synthetic cyclic heptapeptide analog of α-melanocyte-stimulating hormone (α-MSH) that was developed specifically for treating sexual dysfunction. Originally derived from the tanning peptide Melanotan II, PT-141 was designed to retain the sexual arousal effects while eliminating the unwanted pigmentation and other side effects.",
