        "summary": "An investigational once-weekly triple agonist targeting GIP, GLP-1, and glucagon receptors. Lilly reported Phase 3 topline average weight-loss results of up to 20.8% at 80 weeks in TRIUMPH-2 and up to 22.6% at 80 weeks in TRIUMPH-3. The complete trial reports have not yet been peer reviewed, and retatrutide is not FDA approved.",
        "evidence": "strong-human. Retatrutide has published controlled Phase II evidence and sponsor-reported Phase 3 topline results while it remains investigational. In TRIUMPH-2 (NCT05929079), 1,152 adults with type 2 diabetes and obesity or overweight were randomized; Lilly reported average body-weight changes at 80 weeks of -12.7% with 4 mg, -19.1% with 9 mg, and -20.8% with 12 mg, compared with -4.0% with placebo. In TRIUMPH-3 (NCT05882045), 1,949 adults with severe obesity and established cardiovascular disease, with or without type 2 diabetes, were randomized; Lilly reported average body-weight changes at 80 weeks of -21.6% with 9 mg and -22.6% with 12 mg, compared with -3.2% with placebo. These are company-reported topline results and have not yet been published as complete peer-reviewed trial reports; the registry records confirm trial identity and design but do not currently provide posted results. TRIUMPH-3 included exploratory/event analyses of major cardiovascular events, but the reported estimates were imprecise and do not establish cardiovascular-event reduction.",
        "halfLife": "Human pharmacokinetic half-life has not been established in this record.",
