        "summary": "Retatrutide is an investigational triple hormone receptor agonist, developed by Eli Lilly, that simultaneously activates the GIP, GLP-1, and glucagon receptors. It produced the largest pharmacological weight loss recorded to date in a phase 2 trial (24.2% at 48 weeks). It is NOT yet FDA-approved -- it remains in phase 3 (the TRIUMPH program) as of this review, and claims of approval circulating in some vendor/marketing material are inaccurate. Retatrutide (LY3437943) is a synthetic ~39-amino-acid peptide built on a GIP receptor agonist backbone, engineered to also activate the GLP-1 and glucagon receptors, making it the first-in-class 'triple G' (GIP/GLP-1/glucagon) agonist. It binds human GCGR, GIPR, and GLP-1R with reported EC50 values of 5.79, 0.0643, and 0.775 nM respectively.",
