        "evidence": "Application Specific Agent Stage Notes PET tumor imaging ⁶⁸Ga-RGD (⁶⁸Ga-NOTA-RGD₂) Clinical use (China approved) Detects αvβ3⁺ tumors and angiogenesis PET imaging ¹⁸F-Alfatide (¹⁸F-RGD) Phase 2/3 Tumor angiogenesis PET tracer Anti-angiogenic (cancer) Cilengitide (c(RGDfV)) Phase 3 (failed, 2014) Did not improve GBM survival Antiplatelet therapy Eptifibatide (RGD mimetic) FDA Approved (1998) αIIbβ3 inhibitor for ACS/PCI Biomaterial coating RGD-functionalized surfaces Clinical use Titanium implants, hydrogels, scaffolds Drug delivery RGD-conjugated nanoparticles Preclinical/Phase 1 Tumor-targeted chemotherapy delivery [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Pierschbacher MD, Ruoslahti E. \"Cell attachment activity of fibronectin can be duplicated by small synthetic fragments of the molecule.\" Nature . 1984;309:30-33. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Stupp R, et al. \"Cilengitide combined with standard treatment for patients with newly diagnosed glioblastoma (CENTRIC).\" Lancet Oncol . 2014;15:1100-1108. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Kapp TG, et al.",
        "halfLife": "",
