        "mechanism": "Integrin Binding : RGD motif engages the metal-ion-dependent adhesion site (MIDAS) in integrin β-subunits → competitive inhibition of ECM protein binding αvβ3 Targeting : Cyclic RGD peptides preferentially bind αvβ3 integrin - highly expressed on angiogenic endothelium and tumor cells Anti-Angiogenic : αvβ3 blockade inhibits endothelial cell migration, tube formation, and tumor neovascularization Anti-Metastatic : Disrupts integrin-mediated tumor cell adhesion to ECM → inhibits invasion and metastasis Pro-Apoptotic : Integrin detachment triggers anoikis (detachment-induced apoptosis) in anchorage-dependent cells Cell Adhesion Promotion : When immobilized on surfaces, RGD peptides PROMOTE cell attachment (opposite effect to soluble RGD) → basis for biomaterial applications αIIbβ3 Inhibition : RGD mimetics (eptifibatide, tirofiban) block platelet aggregation → approved antiplatelet drugs",
