        "evidence": "Potent HDAC Inhibition : IC50 values in low nanomolar range (HDAC1: 36 nM, HDAC2: 47 nM) T-Cell Lymphoma Efficacy : Clinically meaningful response rates in heavily pretreated CTCL and PTCL patients Durable Responses : Median duration of response ~15 months in CTCL; some patients achieve lasting complete remissions Epigenetic Reactivation : Restores expression of silenced tumor suppressor genes Class I Selectivity : More selective than pan-HDAC inhibitors, potentially reducing off-target toxicity Natural Product Origin : Unique peptide-based structure with optimized drug-like properties Design : Single-arm, open-label, 96 patients with CTCL (Stage IB-IVA) who had received ≥1 prior systemic therapy Dosing : 14 mg/m² IV on days 1, 8, and 15 of 28-day cycle Overall Response Rate (ORR) : 34% (4% CR, 30% PR) Median Duration of Response : 15.0 months Pruritus Relief : Significant reduction in pruritus in 67% of responders (major quality-of-life benefit) Design : 131 patients with relapsed/refractory PTCL ORR : 25% (15% CR/CRu, 10% PR) Median Duration of CR : Not reached at data cutoff",
