        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Selank Chemical name Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro Molecular formula C₃₃H₅₇N₁₁O₉ Molecular weight 751.9 g/mol CAS number 129954-34-3 Sequence Thr-Lys-Pro-Arg-Pro-Gly-Pro Length 7 amino acids Source Synthetic tuftsin analog Half-life 2-8 hours Targets GABA, serotonin, dopamine systems Bioavailability Intranasal, subcutaneous injection Legal status Prescription medication (Russia), research compound elsewhere Selank is a synthetic heptapeptide analog of the immunomodulatory peptide tuftsin, developed in Russia in the 1990s for the treatment of anxiety and cognitive disorders. The peptide was designed to combine the anxiolytic properties of benzodiazepines with cognitive enhancement effects, while avoiding the dependency and tolerance issues associated with traditional anti-anxiety medications.",
