          "Gastrointestinal symptoms dominate the side effect profile. Clinical trials report these frequencies: Nausea: Affects 40-45% of users, usually worst during dose escalation Diarrhea: Occurs in approximately 30% of users Vomiting: Reported by 25% of users, primarily during titration Constipation: Affects roughly 25% of.",
          "Certain side effects require immediate medical evaluation: Pancreatitis: Severe, persistent abdominal pain radiating to the back accompanied by vomiting may indicate pancreatic inflammation. This rare but serious condition requires immediate medical care.",
          "The FDA has issued warnings about compounded semaglutide products. Because compounded medications don't undergo FDA approval processes, their quality, purity, and potency can vary. Some compounding pharmacies use semaglutide salt forms rather than the base form used in approved products, which may affect dosing.",
          "Semaglutide has been used for diabetes since 2017 and weight management since 2021, providing several years of real-world safety data. No unexpected long-term signals have emerged, though surveillance continues.",
          "StatPearls - NCBI Bookshelf (2024)."
