        "mechanism": "11 How Intranasal Semax Research Works Semax is a synthetic heptapeptide based on the ACTH(4-10) sequence and was developed without the hormonal activity of full-length ACTH. Published research has examined neurotrophic signaling, attention, memory, and condition-specific neurological outcomes [1] [3] [7] . Intranasal delivery places a measured solution on the nasal mucosa, which is the route used in the human studies summarized on this page. The calculation is concentration based. Dividing 5,000 mcg by the measured final volume gives mcg per mL. Multiplying that concentration by the verified pump output gives mcg per spray.",
