        "summary": "Semax is a synthetic heptapeptide (Met-Glu-His-Phe-Pro-Gly-Pro) derived from the 4-10 fragment of adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH) - specifically the portion responsible for ACTH's nootropic and neuroprotective effects, stripped of its adrenal-stimulating activity. Developed in Russia by the Institute of Molecular Genetics of the Russian Academy of Sciences and approved in Russia and Ukraine as a prescription drug for stroke treatment, cognitive decline, and optic nerve disease, Semax remains one of the most clinically validated neuropeptides in this database. Its primary mechanism of action is dual: first, it directly stimulates the TrkB receptor (the high-affinity receptor for BDNF, Brain-Derived Neurotrophic Factor), producing downstream CREB phosphorylation, synaptic plasticity gene expression, and neuronal survival signaling.",
