        "evidence": "moderate. Sermorelin (GHRH(1-29)-NH₂) has documented human pharmacodynamic activity: intravenous administration produces dose-dependent growth-hormone release in normal men, with a reported IV disappearance half-time of approximately 4.3 minutes (Barron et al. 1985; Soule et al. 1994). Prolonged subcutaneous infusion promoted growth in children with partial GH insufficiency over one year (Brain et al. 1990). As Geref, sermorelin was historically FDA-approved; the marketed product was voluntarily withdrawn, and FDA determined the withdrawal was not for reasons of safety or effectiveness. This historical regulatory status and documented human pharmacodynamic data do not establish clinical benefit for adult anti-aging, longevity, sleep, or body-composition claims in contemporary compounded formulations.",
