        "evidence": "Published March 4, 2026 Updated August 29, 2026 Quick Brief Complete sermorelin guide: dosage (200500mcg), benefits, side effects, before and after timelines, plus comparisons to ipamorelin and tesamorelin. Sermorelin: Dosage, Benefits, Side Effects & Before and After (2026) Procurement Sermorelin (10MG) Ships from USA $36.00 $72.00 Get Sermorelin (10MG) - with PEPTIDEDECK Sermorelin has quietly become one of the most talked-about peptides in the anti-aging and performance optimization space and for good reason. Unlike synthetic HGH injections that bypass your body's natural hormone feedback loops, sermorelin works with your pituitary gland to restore youthful growth hormone output. The result is a more physiological, safer approach to GH optimization with a compelling body of research behind it. This guide covers everything: what sermorelin is, how it works, the correct sermorelin dosage protocol, realistic sermorelin before and after expectations, sermorelin side effects , and detailed comparisons to ipamorelin and tesamorelin so you can make an informed decision.",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "Understanding the difference between sermorelin and recombinant human growth hormone (rHGH) is critical. They are not the same thing, and the distinction matters both for safety and for how your body responds. Direct HGH injections (e.g., synthetic somatropin) flood the bloodstream with exogenous GH, bypassing the pituitary entirely. This creates a non-physiological spike in IGF-1 and GH levels that can suppress the hypothalamic-pituitary axis over time meaning your body down-regulates its own GH production. Side effects like carpal tunnel syndrome, acromegaly-like features, and insulin resistance are more common at higher doses. Sermorelin , by contrast, acts upstream: it stimulates your pituitary to release GH in natural pulses, preserving the body's negative feedback mechanisms. The pituitary \"decides\" how much GH to release based on your somatostatin levels and overall hormonal milieu, which provides a built-in safety ceiling. You cannot easily overdose the pituitary into acromegaly with a GHRH analogue because the somatostatin feedback system remains intact.",
