        "summary": "SHLP2 (Small Humanin-Like Peptide 2) is a 20-amino acid mitochondria-encoded peptide discovered in 2016 by researchers at the USC Davis School of Gerontology, encoded within the 12S ribosomal RNA region of the mitochondrial genome - the same genomic locus that encodes Humanin. SHLP2 belongs to the SHLP family (SHLP1-6), all sharing structural homology with Humanin but exerting distinct biological profiles. SHLP2's primary mechanisms include cytoprotection against oxidative stress-induced cell death (analogous to Humanin's protective effect), regulation of anabolic hormone signaling - it modulates IGF-1 responsiveness and improves insulin sensitivity in aging models - and mitochondrial quality maintenance. SHLP2 levels decline measurably with age, paralleling Humanin's age-related decline and suggesting a coordinated mitochondrial aging response.",
