        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia SHU-9119 Chemical name SHU-9119 (Ac-Nle-c[Asp-His-D-Nal(2')-Arg-Trp-Lys]-NH₂) Molecular formula C₅₆H₇₃N₁₃O₉ Molecular weight 1,072.3 g/mol CAS number 161854-98-0 Sequence Ac-Nle⁴-c[Asp⁵-His⁶-D-Nal(2')⁷-Arg⁸-Trp⁹-Lys¹⁰]-NH₂ Length 7 amino acids (cyclic, heavily modified) Source Synthetic Half-life ~2-4 hours (estimated from in vivo studies) Targets MC3R antagonist + MC4R antagonist; MC1R partial agonist; MC5R agonist Bioavailability ICV injection (research - does not cross BBB well) Legal status Research compound (not approved) SHU-9119 is a synthetic cyclic melanocortin peptide that serves as the most widely used pharmacological tool for studying melanocortin receptor function - specifically as a potent MC3R and MC4R antagonist. Developed by Victor Hruby's laboratory at the University of Arizona, SHU-9119 has been instrumental in establishing the critical role of MC3R/MC4R in energy homeostasis, feeding behavior, and sexual function.",
        "evidence": "Research Area SHU-9119 Use Key Findings Energy homeostasis ICV injection (1-5 nmol) Establishes MC4R as critical anorexia mediator Leptin signaling Co-administered with leptin Proves leptin→POMC→MC4R pathway Sexual function ICV or intracavernous Blocks melanocortin-induced erection; establishes MC4R role Inflammatory response Peripheral or central Partially blocks anti-inflammatory melanocortin effects Cachexia models ICV Reverses cancer cachexia-associated anorexia Agouti/AgRP biology Tool compound Validates AgRP as endogenous MC4R antagonist analog [ 1 ] [ 2 ] [ 3 ] ↑ 1.0 1.1 Hruby VJ, et al. \"Cyclic lactam α-melanotropin analogues of Ac-Nle⁴-c[Asp⁵,D-Phe⁷,Lys¹⁰]α-MSH(4-10)-NH₂ with bulky aromatic amino acids at position 7 show high antagonist potency.\" J Med Chem . 1995;38:3454-3461. ↑ 2.0 2.1 Fan W, et al. \"Role of melanocortinergic neurons in feeding and the agouti obesity syndrome.\" Nature . 1997;385:165-168. ↑ 3.0 3.1 Cone RD. \"Anatomy and regulation of the central melanocortin system.\" Nat Neurosci . 2005;8:571-578.",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "MC4R Antagonism : Blocks α-MSH and other melanocortin agonist binding at MC4R → prevents anorexigenic signaling → increases food intake and body weight MC3R Antagonism : Blocks MC3R signaling → disrupts nutrient partitioning and energy homeostasis MC1R Partial Agonism : Retains agonist activity at MC1R - can stimulate melanogenesis (does not block pigmentation) MC5R Agonism : Full agonist at MC5R (sebaceous gland function, immune modulation) Orexigenic Effect : ICV SHU-9119 increases food intake by 50-200% in rodents by blocking endogenous melanocortin tone Blocks Leptin Anorexia : SHU-9119 blocks the appetite-suppressing effects of leptin, demonstrating that leptin signals through the melanocortin pathway Sexual Function : MC4R antagonism blocks melanocortin-induced penile erection - establishes MC4R role in sexual response Cyclic Structure : Lactam bridge between Asp⁵ and Lys¹⁰ constrains the peptide for optimal receptor interaction",
