        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Sigumir is a Khavinson cytomedin - peptide complex A-4 - extracted from the bone and cartilage tissue of young animals, developed at the St. Petersburg Institute of Bioregulation and Gerontology as the skeletal tissue bioregulator of the Khavinson framework. It works by delivering an organ-specific peptide signal directly to osteoblasts (the cells that build bone matrix) and chondrocytes (the cells that maintain cartilage), normalizing the gene expression programs that govern how these cells produce collagen, regulate bone remodeling, and maintain joint integrity. In practical terms, Sigumir tells aging bone and cartilage cells to behave more like young ones - restoring the balance between bone formation and resorption that tips toward net bone loss in osteoporosis, and maintaining the cartilage matrix synthesis that slows in osteoarthritis.",
        "evidence": "Peptide University labels its records as aggregated from empirical research and anecdotal community data. This record is retained as supplied and is not upgraded to clinical evidence.",
        "halfLife": "",
        "halfLifeContext": "",
        "mechanism": "Sigumir is a Khavinson cytomedin - peptide complex A-4 - extracted from the bone and cartilage tissue of young animals, developed at the St. Petersburg Institute of Bioregulation and Gerontology as the skeletal tissue bioregulator of the Khavinson framework. It works by delivering an organ-specific peptide signal directly to osteoblasts (the cells that build bone matrix) and chondrocytes (the cells that maintain cartilage), normalizing the gene expression programs that govern how these cells produce collagen, regulate bone remodeling, and maintain joint integrity. In practical terms, Sigumir tells aging bone and cartilage cells to behave more like young ones - restoring the balance between bone formation and resorption that tips toward net bone loss in osteoporosis, and maintaining the cartilage matrix synthesis that slows in osteoarthritis.",
        "limitations": [
          "Bone malignancy (primary or metastatic) - osteoblast gene program normalization and bone matrix synthesis stimulation in the context of malignant bone involvement has not been characterized; bone metastases from prostate, breast, or other primary tumors require oncological evaluation before any bone bioregulator use.",
          "Osteosarcoma or chondrosarcoma - direct contraindication; malignant bone and cartilage cell gene program normalization activity is not established.",
          "Active bone infection (osteomyelitis) - bioregulator activity at the bone tissue level during active bacterial bone infection has not been characterized; antimicrobial management takes priority.",
          "Paget's disease of bone with active high bone turnover phase - the dysregulated coupled bone remodeling of Paget's disease creates an unpredictable context for osteoblast bioregulator normalization; requires specialist evaluation.",
          "Known hypersensitivity to Sigumir (bone and cartilage tissue cytomedin peptide complex) or formulation excipients (including gelatin capsule).",
          "Pregnancy - bone and cartilage remodeling during pregnancy involves significant hormonal regulation (relaxin, estrogen, PTH-rP); exogenous skeletal bioregulator activity has not been evaluated in this context.",
          "Concurrent teriparatide therapy without specialist supervision - teriparatide's direct PTH receptor-mediated osteoblast stimulation combined with Sigumir's osteoblast gene program normalization creates an additive pro-anabolic skeletal effect; beneficial but should be initiated under specialist oversight in subjects",
          "Hypercalcemia of any cause - bone formation stimulation in the context of elevated baseline calcium may worsen hypercalcemia; calcium levels should be normalized before initiating Sigumir."
        ],
