        "summary": "SIA-31-C18 (Single Regulator) is a 31-amino acid GLP-1 receptor agonist belonging to the Peptide Receptor Modulator Research Series. It is a semaglutide-class single incretin agonist featuring a C18 fatty diacid (octadecanedioyl) side chain attached via a γ-Glu-2x AEEA linker at Lys20, enabling albumin binding and extended half-life comparable to once-weekly dosing formats. The backbone closely mirrors the GLP-1 incretin sequence with Aib (alpha-aminoisobutyric acid) substitutions at key positions for DPP-4 resistance and enhanced receptor affinity. CAS: 910463-68-2. Structurally analogous in class to semaglutide. Once-weekly subcutaneous injection. Key reference literature: Wilding et al. (NEJM 2021) - once-weekly semaglutide in adults with overweight or obesity, 15% mean weight loss at 68 weeks; Lincoff et al. (NEJM 2023) - semaglutide and cardiovascular outcomes in obesity without diabetes; Perkovic et al. (NEJM 2024) - semaglutide effects on chronic kidney disease.",
