        "summary": "A key neuropeptide involved in pain transmission, inflammation, and mood regulation, and the target of the first neuropeptide receptor antagonist drug.",
        "evidence": "Strong human evidence Endogenous neuropeptide involved in pain and neurogenic inflammation. Not a medicine; NK1-receptor antagonists (e.g. aprepitant) are licensed UK antiemetics that work against Substance P signalling. Human evidence grade A, Strong human evidence. Citation quality grade A, Strong human evidence.",
