        "summary": "Taxorest is a Khavinson cytomedin - peptide complex A-19 - extracted from the bronchial mucosal tissue of young animals, developed as the oral bronchopulmonary bioregulator of the Khavinson framework and the commercial cytomedin counterpart to Bronchogen (the injectable synthetic tetrapeptide Ala-Glu-Asp-Leu). It delivers a mixture of bronchial tissue-derived low-molecular-weight peptides that interact with bronchial epithelial cells at the transcriptional level, normalizing the gene expression programs governing ciliary function, mucus composition and production, barrier integrity, anti-inflammatory secretory profiles, and the regenerative capacity of bronchial epithelial progenitor cells. In practical terms, Taxorest signals aging airway epithelial cells to restore the protective, self-cleaning respiratory surface that years of accumulated environmental, inflammatory, or infectious damage have progressively eroded.",
