        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia TB-500 Chemical name Thymosin Beta-4 Fragment (17-23) Molecular formula C₂₁₂H₃₅₀N₅₆O₇₈S Molecular weight 4963.4 g/mol CAS number 77591-33-4 Sequence Full Thymosin Beta-4 sequence (43 amino acids) Length 43 amino acids Source Synthetic analog of naturally occurring Thymosin Beta-4 Half-life 2-4 hours Targets G-actin, cell migration, angiogenesis Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status Research compound only TB-500 is a synthetic analog of Thymosin Beta-4, a naturally occurring peptide found in high concentrations in blood platelets, wound fluid, and other tissues involved in healing. TB-500 contains the active sequence (amino acids 17-23) responsible for actin binding, cell migration, and wound healing, making it one of the most potent healing and regenerative compounds available.",
        "evidence": "Muscle Injuries : Faster recovery from strains, tears, and exercise-induced damage Tendon/Ligament Repair : Enhanced healing of notoriously slow-healing connective tissues Joint Health : Improved cartilage repair and reduced joint inflammation Cardiac Tissue : Potential protective effects on heart muscle and blood vessels Neurological Repair : May support nerve regeneration and neuroplasticity Skin Healing : Improved wound healing with reduced scarring Cardiac Protection : Potential protective effects against heart damage Blood Vessel Health : Promotes healthy blood vessel formation and function Circulation Enhancement : Improved blood flow to tissues Endothelial Function : Better blood vessel lining health and function Wound Healing Studies : Investigation for diabetic ulcers and chronic wounds Cardiac Research : Studies on heart attack recovery and cardiac protection Neurological Research : Investigation for stroke recovery and neurodegenerative diseases Ophthalmology : Research for corneal injury healing and dry eye syndrome Diabetic Ulcers : Accelerated healing of chronic",
