        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Teduglutide Chemical name [Gly²]-GLP-2(1-33) Molecular formula C₁₆₄H₂₅₂N₄₄O₅₅S Molecular weight 3752 g/mol CAS number 197922-42-2 Sequence HGDGSFSDEMNTILDNLAARDFINWLIQTKITD Length 33 amino acids Source Recombinant (E. coli) Half-life ~2 hours (vs 7 min for native GLP-2) Targets GLP-2 receptor agonist Bioavailability ~88% (subcutaneous) Legal status FDA Approved (2012) Teduglutide (brand name Gattex in the US, Revestive in Europe) is a recombinant analog of human glucagon-like peptide-2 (GLP-2) approved for the treatment of short bowel syndrome (SBS) in adults and pediatric patients aged 1 year and older who are dependent on parenteral support. Developed by NPS Pharmaceuticals (now Takeda), teduglutide represents the first and only GLP-2 receptor agonist approved for clinical use.",
