          "Orthostatic hypotension: Dizziness and tachycardia may occur within 4 hours of injection, particularly with initial doses (5% incidence). Nausea: Reported in 8% of patients. Headache: 8% incidence. Leg cramps: 3% incidence. Dizziness: 8% incidence.",
          "Osteosarcoma (theoretical): Boxed warning based on dose-dependent osteosarcoma observed in rats exposed to high doses for near-lifetime duration. This risk has not been demonstrated in humans; post-marketing surveillance (over 2 million patient-years) has not identified an increased risk.",
