        "summary": "Testagen is a synthetic tetrapeptide (Lys-Glu-Asp-Gly) Khavinson bioregulator derived from testicular tissue polypeptide extracts - identified as the bioactive core sequence responsible for the Leydig cell regulatory, testosterone synthesis-supporting, and testicular tissue-normalizing activity of the native testicular extract. The testes perform two biologically distinct and equally essential functions: endocrine secretion (testosterone production by Leydig cells in the testicular interstitium, regulated by LH from the anterior pituitary) and spermatogenesis (production of mature spermatozoa by the seminiferous tubule system, involving Sertoli cells and regulated by both FSH and intratesticular testosterone).",
