        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia TGF-beta1 Chemical name Transforming Growth Factor Beta 1 Molecular formula C₅₅₃H₈₆₈N₁₅₂O₁₆₀S₈ Molecular weight 25,000 g/mol (active homodimer) CAS number 59399-46-1 Sequence 112 amino acids per monomer; disulfide-linked homodimer Length 112 amino acids (mature monomer) Source Endogenous (platelets, macrophages, most cell types); recombinant Half-life ~2-3 minutes (circulating) Targets TGFβRI (ALK5), TGFβRII → Smad2/3 pathway Bioavailability Minimal systemic use (local tissue effects) Legal status Research compound (anti-TGF-β therapies in clinical trials) TGF-β1 ( Transforming Growth Factor Beta 1 ) is the prototype of the TGF-β superfamily, one of the most important cytokine families in biology. TGF-β1 is a 25 kDa homodimeric protein with profound and context-dependent effects on cell growth, differentiation, apoptosis, immune regulation, and extracellular matrix production.",
