        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Published June 5, 2026 Updated August 25, 2026 Quick Brief What does Zepbound (tirzepatide) actually do over 72 weeks? This guide replaces hype photos with published SURMOUNT trial data: a month-by-month timeline, an effect-size table in real pounds and kilograms, the head-to-head vs Wegovy, and what happens to your results if you stop. Zepbound Before and After: Real Results, Weight Loss Timeline & Reviews (2026) Procurement Embody Compounded Tirzepatide Ships from USA Start Tirzepatide - $119/mo Search for \"Zepbound before and after\" and you will find thousands of dramatic transformation photos, but very few that tell you what is actually typical, what the clinical trials measured, and how long it took. This guide separates the marketing-grade success stories from the real, published numbers.",
        "evidence": "The honest answer is yes, and the evidence is unusually strong. Zepbound is the obesity brand of tirzepatide, a once-weekly injection that activates two gut-hormone receptors at once, GIP and GLP-1, which is why it is described as a dual agonist. The FDA approved it for chronic weight management in adults with obesity (BMI 30 or higher) or overweight (BMI 27 or higher) plus a weight-related condition such as high blood pressure, type 2 diabetes, dyslipidemia, obstructive sleep apnea, or cardiovascular disease. [2] The \"before and after\" results everyone references come mainly from the SURMOUNT clinical program. In SURMOUNT-1 , a 72-week trial of 2,539 adults with obesity or overweight (without type 2 diabetes), average weight reduction was 16.0% on the 5 mg dose, 21.4% on 10 mg, and 22.5% on 15 mg, compared with just 2.4% in the placebo group. [1] [3] Even more striking, 36% (10 mg) and 40% (15 mg) of participants lost at least 25% of their starting body weight, versus essentially nobody on placebo.",
