        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Tirzepatide Chemical name Dual GIP/GLP-1 receptor agonist Molecular formula C₂₂₅H₃₄₈N₄₈O₆₈ Molecular weight 4813.45 g/mol CAS number 2023788-19-2 Sequence 39-amino acid synthetic peptide with C20 fatty diacid Length 39 amino acids Source Synthetic GIP/GLP-1 analog Half-life ~5 days Targets GIP and GLP-1 receptors Bioavailability Subcutaneous injection Legal status FDA approved for T2D and obesity (Mounjaro/Zepbound) Tirzepatide is a first-in-class dual glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide (GIP) and glucagon-like peptide-1 (GLP-1) receptor agonist that represents a breakthrough in metabolic medicine. FDA-approved as Mounjaro for type 2 diabetes and as Zepbound for chronic weight management, tirzepatide has demonstrated unprecedented weight loss results in clinical trials, with participants losing up to 22.5% of body weight.",
