        "summary": "TIA-39-C20 (Triple Regulator) is a 39-amino acid triple incretin agonist belonging to the Peptide Receptor Modulator Research Series. It simultaneously activates three receptors: the GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R), the GIP receptor (GIPR), and the glucagon receptor (GCGR). This triple mechanism adds glucagon receptor activation on top of dual incretin agonism - glucagon signaling directly increases resting energy expenditure and hepatic fat oxidation, producing weight loss effects beyond appetite suppression alone. Features a C20 fatty diacid (eicosanedioyl) side chain via a γ-Glu-2x AEEA linker for albumin binding and extended once-weekly half-life. CAS: 2381089-83-2. Structurally analogous in class to retatrutide. Once-weekly subcutaneous injection. Key reference literature: Jastreboff et al. (NEJM 2023) - triple-hormone-receptor agonist Phase 2 obesity trial (24.2% weight loss at 48 weeks); Sanyal et al. (Nature Medicine 2024) - retatrutide for MASLD; Rosenstock et al.",
