        "sourceId": "peptidehub",
        "url": "https://peptidehub.bio/peptides/triptorelin",
        "lastReviewed": "Not stated",
        "summary": "Triptorelin is a long-acting synthetic GnRH (gonadotropin-releasing hormone) agonist decapeptide with approximately 100 times the receptor binding potency of native GnRH. Triptorelin's primary research application in the peptide community is HPG (hypothalamic-pituitary-gonadal) axis restart after suppression from exogenous testosterone (TRT) or anabolic androgen use - a protocol where a single low dose (0.1mg) triggers a powerful initial LH and FSH flare response by massively stimulating pituitary GnRH receptors before the agonist-induced downregulation of those receptors occurs. This flare effect is exploited in restart protocols because an HPG-suppressed axis responds to the initial GnRH surge with a compensatory LH spike that stimulates Leydig cell testosterone production. In sustained use (as in prostate cancer treatment), continuous GnRH agonism causes receptor downregulation and hormonal castration - the opposite of the restart effect.",
        "evidence": "Protocol-focused educational summary. Linked papers, site-listed ranges and commercial context are retained with source attribution.",
