        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia Triptorelin Chemical name Triptorelin; [D-Trp⁶]-GnRH; Triptorelin pamoate (Trelstar) Molecular formula C₆₄H₈₂N₁₈O₁₃ Molecular weight 1311.5 g/mol CAS number 57773-63-4 Sequence pGlu-His-Trp-Ser-Tyr-D-Trp-Leu-Arg-Pro-Gly-NH₂ Length 10 amino acids (decapeptide) Source Synthetic analog of gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH) Half-life 3-5 hours (free peptide); extended release formulations: weeks to months Targets Gonadotropin-releasing hormone receptor (GnRHR) Bioavailability Intramuscular depot injection; ~95% absorption from depot Legal status FDA-approved (Trelstar, Triptodur); prescription only Triptorelin is a synthetic decapeptide analog of endogenous gonadotropin-releasing hormone (GnRH, also known as luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone or LHRH).",
        "evidence": "Triptorelin has been evaluated in multiple large clinical trials for advanced prostate cancer: A pooled analysis of three registration trials (N=428) demonstrated that 91.2-97.7% of patients achieved medical castration by day 29, with 93.3-96.2% maintaining castration throughout the study period. The TROG 96.01 trial demonstrated that addition of androgen deprivation therapy (including triptorelin) to radiation therapy for locally advanced prostate cancer significantly improved overall survival compared to radiation alone. Non-inferiority trials have confirmed that triptorelin achieves comparable testosterone suppression to leuprolide and goserelin. Store lyophilized powder at −20°C, desiccated Reconstituted solutions in sterile water are stable for up to 1 week at 4°C For long-term storage of reconstituted solutions, aliquot and store at −20°C Stable for up to 12 months as lyophilized powder at −20°C [ 2 ] ↑ Crawford ED, Tombal B, Miller K, et al.",
