          "Tumor flare: Initial testosterone surge can cause acute worsening of prostate cancer symptoms (bone pain, urinary obstruction, spinal cord compression). Anti-androgen cover (e.g., bicalutamide) for the first 2-4 weeks is recommended.",
          "Known hypersensitivity to triptorelin, GnRH, or GnRH agonist analogs Pregnancy (Category X; may cause fetal harm) Women who are or may become pregnant Patients with undiagnosed abnormal vaginal bleeding."
