        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "Ventfort is a Khavinson cytomedin - peptide complex A-3 - extracted from vascular tissue of young animals, developed as the oral vascular endothelial bioregulator of the Khavinson framework. The vascular endothelium is the single cell layer lining every blood vessel in the body, and it does far more than passive containment - it actively regulates vessel tone through nitric oxide production, controls clotting through thrombomodulin and tPA expression, governs inflammatory cell adhesion through ICAM-1 and VCAM-1, and directs angiogenesis through VEGF signaling. Ventfort delivers a multi-peptide vascular tissue extract that interacts with endothelial cell nuclear receptors to normalize the gene expression programs governing these functions - in plain terms, it signals aging, dysfunctional endothelial cells to restore the protective, anti-inflammatory, vasodilatory phenotype they had when young.",
