        "mechanism": "nAChR Competitive Antagonism : Competes with acetylcholine for binding at the postsynaptic nicotinic receptor → prevents muscle depolarization → reduced contraction force Post-Synaptic Action : Acts on the receptor side (muscle), not the nerve side - complementary to presynaptic agents like Argireline Dose-Dependent : Higher concentrations provide greater muscle relaxation within cosmetic safety limits Reversible : Competitive antagonism is fully reversible - muscle function returns completely when peptide is washed off or metabolized No Systemic Effect : Topical application at cosmetic concentrations does not produce systemic neuromuscular blockade",
