        "lastReviewed": "2026-09-17",
        "summary": "From Wikipep - The Peptide Encyclopedia VIP (Vasoactive Intestinal Peptide) Chemical name Vasoactive Intestinal Polypeptide Molecular formula C₁₄₇H₂₃₈N₄₄O₄₂S Molecular weight 3326.82 g/mol CAS number 37221-79-7 Sequence His-Ser-Asp-Ala-Val-Phe-Thr-Asp-Asn-Tyr-Thr-Arg-Leu-Arg-Lys-Gln-Met-Ala-Val-Lys-Lys-Tyr-Leu-Asn-Ser-Ile-Leu-Asn-NH₂ Length 28 amino acids Source Endogenous neuropeptide/Synthetic Half-life 1-2 minutes (plasma), 20 minutes (tissue) Targets VPAC1, VPAC2, PAC1 receptors Bioavailability Intranasal, subcutaneous, nebulized Legal status Research compound/Compounded medication VIP (Vasoactive Intestinal Peptide) is a 28-amino acid neuropeptide hormone that functions as a potent anti-inflammatory, immunomodulator, and neuroprotective agent throughout the body. Originally discovered in the intestinal tract, VIP is now recognized as one of the most important regulatory peptides in human physiology, with receptors found in virtually every organ system.",
